{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes","id":9451,"title":"Lunar Craft Themes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T21:22:14-08:00","id":9451,"title":"Lunar Craft Themes","content":"As a bridge to 3E for Lunars (which is looking to be 2-3 years out from the time I write this) what *are* the themes of Lunars? I've become so lost over the course of 2E. <br /> <br /> I feel each Exalt should have a path to the different mechanics of the game. Sidereals follow visions scoured from the Loom itself to aid in crafting. Dragon Bloods are able to create great wonders that resonate with their elemental property. I could think of several charms for each of those splats....<br /> <br /> However, when I come to Lunars, I am lost. Making things is about permanance, a lasting mark. This can match up with the survival and warden themes to a degree...but the mecurial and ever changing nature of the Moonkin not so much. Appealing to the Wyld themes - I feel that both 3E is going to abandon them to the Fay and that it does not lend itself well to direct crafting (vision quest to your hearts content). Lunars are neither the Animal Exalted nor would those themes aid in any way. Autochthon choose man because of their capability for Faith, Dogma, and *Tools*. Animals had no tools and pretty much suck at building things compared to man kind. <br /> <br /> I don't even feel I grasp the theme of the Lunar any more. All we know thus far is Rage? That they can shapeshift? These are not themes - at least ones that I could adapt to the mechanics of Sorcery, Crafting, or most (but not all) social interactions? <br /> <br /> I'm just curious and a bit flustered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T21:34:22-08:00","id":9453,"title":"","content":"Well, Zatesh's reversed scythe have to come from somewhere, probably involve eating a bunch of Othermoons and then shit-out Artifact from his moon-ass :v","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T01:08:20-08:00","id":9526,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Solars make the BEST of whatever they design. The best sword, the most beautiful robes, the manse with the coolest hearthstone, etc.<br /> <br /> A Lunar on the other hand can MacGuyver anything out of anything, or make things with great versatility. A sword that is also a whip, a cannonball that births more cannonballs when fired, or robes whose edges are as sharp as blades. They'll take a tree branch and, while fighting you, stick it into a rock and suddenly pull a goremaul out of the earth. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> A disclaimer: I can't remember any of the Lunar craft Charms right now, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:11:47-08:00","id":9618,"title":"","content":"There ain't no such thing like a &quot;Lunar Craft&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:03:57-08:00","id":9651,"title":"","content":"Lunars improvise, yes. They make temporary things that are perfect for the moment, and they adapt existing things to unintended uses. Wonders forged by the magics of the Lunars are multi-purpose, inobvious or cleverly outside-the-box obvious in their application, or made simple but strong. Ornate Lunar wonders are rare, and generally ornate in their utilitarian form. They are useful first. And it is likely they are useful in multiple circumstances rather than being perfect in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:18:25-08:00","id":9661,"title":"","content":"I'm anticipating that the main idea of &quot;alter self rather than environment&quot; means that they prefer to work with their body as a tool. That may be the only thing that can be said about it in absence of a detailed book sitting in front of anyone. Certainly, given that Solars work with all aspects of Craft, one cannot expect them not to be able to formulate quick solutions to issues and work in a short amount of time, so I have doubt in that as a major definition between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:11:28-08:00","id":9797,"title":"","content":"Art is about Creation<br /> <br /> -and my post was eaten :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:50:34-08:00","id":9877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9661#post9661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm anticipating that the main idea of &quot;alter self rather than environment&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does this idea come from? I haven't seen any developer comment to this effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly, given that Solars work with all aspects of Craft, one cannot expect them not to be able to formulate quick solutions to issues and work in a short amount of time, so I have doubt in that as a major definition between the two. </div> </div> </div>Solars absolutely HAVE to have Glorious McGuyering Method as a Charm or set of Charms, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:22:53-08:00","id":9902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9877#post9877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does this idea come from? I haven't seen any developer comment to this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also haven't seen anything direct. I presume Saur Ops's interpreting the physicality emphasis: it's possible Lunar magic doesn't directly alter the environment, but alters the Lunar to better alter the environment. I'd expect to see plenty of this in EX3 Lunars -- it matches all the examples we've gotten -- but I don't think we can say there <i>won't</i> be any direct alteration outside the Lunar. Not yet, at least.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Solars absolutely HAVE to have Glorious McGuyering Method as a Charm or set of Charms, yes. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with both of you. It's not to say Lunars <i>can't</i> <i>also</i> have that kind of thing to play around with, mind. If they do, it will hopefully feel/operate distinctly from the Solar analogues or mean different things in the context of the Lunar Charmset. It's just not gonna happen that Solars will be denied that kind of thing because Lunars have it &quot;locked in.&quot; From what they've said, the devs aren't going for that kind of niche protection.<br /> <br /> Just for fun and discussion aid, I'mma drop in the substantive dev quotes I've pulled together on EX3 Lunars and Crafting (spoilered for space) :<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: <b>(volkmar)</b></i><br /> <i>I was merely curious how does [shapeshifting] help in making daiklaves or repairing the weather controls in Rathess or in any other thing that requires a bit more specialized knowledge than &quot;hammer, nail, hit&quot; assuming a Lunar would not be out of place doing any of those things.</i><br /> <i>I'm also curious if shapeshifting would come into this somewhere. Ie: could you have a &quot;smart&quot; form, maybe taking on demon or spiritual shapes? </i><br /> <br /> A: <b>(Holden)</b><br /> Shapeshifting doesn't help you with those things. (Well, I mean, maybe you could turn into a mouse to crawl inside a sky mantis tower and jigger some delicate parts back into alignment by hand? I dunno. Mostly it doesn't.)<br /> <br /> It's not like Lunars have some kind of special brain damage that makes them less-able to learn things than other Exalts. They can study Lore, Craft, Occult, sure. Their magic isn't the best in the world at building stuff, although they have stuff to help with it. They're certainly not the peers of the Solars in that category or anything (but then, who is?).<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, as a group, Lunars are less dependent on external props than anyone else-- from artifacts to infrastructure-- and this is one reason why they tend to favor simple, robust tools that are either very difficult to break, or which are easy to replace.<br /> <br /> That said, keep in mind-- they have Intelligence Charms. You will, from time to time, see Lunar Tony Stark building amazing shit in a cave, out of scraps. But as a whole they don't trend toward sophisticated big-scale manufacturing projects, in large part because the majority of Lunars don't like doing anything that requires them to set up an immobile and semi-permanent base of operations, like a fully-stocked-and-kitted artificer's workshop. It's more common to see a Lunar set up a temporary work site, build a daiklave or some armor or some similar piece of personal kit for himself or for someone else, and then break down the site, hide any of the components he can't easily replace, and then move on until he needs it again some years later. Most Lunars operate on wartime footing at all times, and they are all priority targets.*<br /> <br /> *There are exceptions to all these things, and they tend to be interesting subjects in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>(Kitsunemimi-Maiden)</b><br /> This is the first thing I've heard of 3e Lunars that truly excites me, as 1e and 2e both liked to pretend Lunars were brain-damaged (since the crafting system was entirely dependent on either uncommonly long downtimes given the 10-year span most games are expected to never breach, or charms to reduce those downtime requirements). I hope this remains a true part of the plan all the way to the 3e Lunar book and beyond, and Sidereals are also capable [Serenity does favor Craft, after all].</i><br /> <br /> <b>(Holden)</b><br /> Mmm. Just keep in mind that I said &quot;amazing shit&quot; rather than &quot;power armor&quot; or &quot;warstriders&quot; intentionally. When you go off the grid, you don't get the benefits of the grid, so to speak. That still leaves the ability to make moonsilver plate, personal weapons, mystic veils, and other such magical wonders well within your capabilities-- and frankly, those things are generally better-suited to Lunar endeavors than something that needs specialist personnel to maintain and repair and a manse to keep it running anyway.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for someone that can outperform a maxed out Solar artifact-crafter-- you're not going to find one. If you're looking to play a Lunar that can make cool artifacts and enhance the story, sure. 3e crafting should be fun, whichever kind of Exalt you're playing.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 11-13-2013, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:51:06-08:00","id":9923,"title":"","content":"So point:<br /> <br /> Art is all about creation. The fundamentals of technique will only carry one so far - after which it becomes a matter of the innate insanity of ones mind and the brilliance of your vision. Both of which rely upon (attributes) rather than (abilities). While I agree some other splats will be better at making sounder armor and sharper swords - it is my *firm* belief that Lunars are better at distilling artistic sensibility into the raw technique of painting/sculpture/so on. While I see Solars as the primary engineers and architects of the First Age roads/bridges/forts and factories - I believe the greatest artists of the First Age had many/mostly Lunars among their number. Who else can see, better, the infinite shapes a block of stone might take or distill the flitting images of a dream onto canvass?<br /> <br /> I think art resonates with the concept of Lunars better than any other splat honestly. <br /> <br /> If you all think turning to yourself for tools is the Lunar plan, and crafting is mostly mental, what kinds of changes to your own mind could you invoke? <br /> <br /> Further, if Lunars are typecast as too insular, such as not making things (that last), it still drives them away from making an impact on the setting. I know this is not the case so I expect the writers have other plans for Lunar craft than just MacGyver. That box would be far too narrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:58:31-08:00","id":9929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9902#post9902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also haven't seen anything direct. I presume Saur Ops's meaning is an interpretation of the physicality emphasis; it's possible Lunar magic may not directly alter the environment, but may alter the Lunar to be better at altering the environment. I'd expect to see plenty of this in EX3 Lunars -- it matches all the examples we've so far gotten -- but I don't think we can yet say there <i>won't</i> be any direct altering of the environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got some posters making reasonable-sounding arguments that Lunars won't even have something like Hybrid Body Rearrangement in 3rd Edition. So there are people arguing against mastery of personal form as well as master of external form.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it depends on what kind of magic we can expect from Barbarian Beast-Gods. Hannuman, rakshasha, kitsune and tanuki and tengu, Godzilla, and other sources which share space with <i>Exalted</i>'s Fair Folk and gods and other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on your quoted developer comments, I could see two Lunar Charms: One for making delicate and fragile things very quickly from anything that's lying around, and the other for working long and hard to create simple tools which are practically indestructible. Either the Lunar wants to make the process of replacing disposable tools as painless as possible, or wants to ensure their long-term investments are as long-term as possible.<br /> <br /> By contrast, a Solar would be more easily capable of making something very quickly, from anything that's lying around, AND ensuring that it's particularly durable for something of its kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Lunar Exalted will have a Charm to take an existing wonder and repurpose it -- perhaps even break it down entirely -- to create a different wonder. But I think Solar Exalted will be better at this -- able to take a truly complex wonder and make an equally complex wonder out of it, if not a superior wonder.<br /> <br /> Though that could easily be a function of Ability-based Charms; naturally, a Solar skilled enough to have the Charm in the first place will be skilled enough to understand and build the most complex of artifacts. The Attribute-based Lunar, on the other hand, might understand how to change a device's form, but won't necessarily understand its function well enough.<br /> <br /> But then, the different Trait-basis for Charms is as much part of the difference between &quot;polished Solar magic&quot; and &quot;rough Lunar magic&quot; as the Charms themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T13:15:36-08:00","id":9938,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.sadanduseless.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/03/397.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T13:35:48-08:00","id":9948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9877#post9877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does this idea come from? I haven't seen any developer comment to this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That time John talked about how there's no such thing as a generic competency that all Exalted require to be worthy of the name, he said something <i>similar</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars? Visceral, magnetic, sexual, physical, mercurial, changing themselves rather than changing the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine Lunars as having Charms that make for some weird crafting methods, like reaching their hands into a thing and having filaments extrude from their fingers to deftly reshape the materials from within.<br /> <br /> I also imagine this will be distinct from the idea of the kinds of things Lunars are likely to make (particularly as pertains to Evocations they can use).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:22:19-08:00","id":10023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes#post9451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel each Exalt should have a path to the different mechanics of the game. Sidereals follow visions scoured from the Loom itself to aid in crafting. Dragon Bloods are able to create great wonders that resonate with their elemental property. I could think of several charms for each of those splats....</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting is also one of &quot;the different mechanics of the game!&quot; If you believe that all Exalted should have paths to all the different mechanics of the game, then you also believe that the game needs a Solar take on shapeshifting or a Dragon-Blooded take on weaving Fate.<br /> <br /> Lunars may have some charms that incidentally help them at crafting, but I don't think that there should be any &quot;Lunar craft charms&quot; -- attempts to shoehorn them in in previous editions have been part of the thinking that led to the bland sameness that infected so much of the 2e Lunar charmset. Different charmsets follow different types of logic; the logic of Lunar magic doesn't (or shouldn't) focus on those kinds of competencies or skills in the way that, say, Solar or Lunar magic does.<br /> <br /> It isn't something that any Lunar fan should <i>want</i> wordcount wasted on in the Lunars book. If you line up the Exalted we know about according to how close crafting fits into their thematics, Lunars are -- literally, no question -- at the very bottom of the list. Solars, Sidereals, DBs, Abyssals, and, in 3e, Infernals are all Ability-based to some extent or another and therefore have a dedicated Craft tree; Solars are explicitly based on skill and human endeavor to an extent, while Abyssals and Infernals are altered Solar shards; Infernals inherit the powers of the makers of the universe; Alchemicals are Attribute-based, but are the chosen of the Great Maker.<br /> <br /> Lunars have nothing. Luna is not a famous crafter, and their charmset is not structured in a way that leads to any particular focus on crafting themes. The reason you can't think of how Lunar craft could work is because it doesn't really fit into their themes at all. Sure, you could force the issue and give Lunars crappy bottom-rung dedicated crafting powers that are, no question, strictly worse than everyone else's (because, again, everyone else has at least some route to crafting in their themes, and Lunars do not), but <i>why</i>? Why do you want that? People happily make numerous Solars who never learn to Craft, and DBs who never learn to craft, and Sidereals and Infernals and Abyssals and Alchemicals who never learn to craft. I don't understand why some Lunar fans feel that access to crafting is important. Nothing in Lunar themes or concepts makes it particularly relevant to being a Lunar; nothing inherent in the Exalted requires that you have access to it (because, again, people happily play numerous Exalted of the other types who never learn it -- in fact, I would say the vast majority of Exalted never learn to craft, even among types like Solars and Alchemicals where the potential is a big deal.)<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Lunar manual should contain a single specific 'crafting charm'; I don't see how it benefits Lunars to include it. Devote the wordcount to something (anything!) else, to developing some other aspect of Lunar power that actually fits their core themes rather than trying to mindlessly ape the themes that were appropriate for other types of Exalted. The different splats are meant to be fundimentally distinct -- they support different types of stories and are focused in different areas. Some of this includes growing in directions or ways that other splats don't; some of this includes, yeah, lacking magical access to areas of expertise and types of charms that other splats have.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that Lunars are <i>unable</i> to craft -- it doesn't even mean they're bad at crafting, as long as you're not comparing them to other Exalted or similar beings. There will be artifacts crafted by Lunars. They can craft better than a mortal, definitely, and better than most gods or spirits, because if nothing else they probably have ways to add dice to the process, and there are probably some ways they can shoehorn their powers into providing some benefit for it, like growing extra arms to work a bit faster or somesuch. In short Lunars can craft the way any superhumanly smart, strong, fast, dexterous magical being with vast control over their physical form could craft, which is still very very good. But these will all be incidental applications for abilities with other focuses as well -- there is no &quot;crafting path&quot; for Lunars inherent in their charmset, and I don't think that Lunars get many, if any, charms specifically dedicated to crafting alone. They can't put their Lunar magic directly into the crafting process itself the way most other Exalted can, because that's not how Lunar magic works.<br /> <br /> Picture a blacksmith who Exalts as a Solar, say. The magic of his Solar Exaltation flows through the paths set by his skill at crafting, making him a supernaturally-skilled crafter, because that's the specific way Solar magic works. That's likely the main focus of his character! He can also expand into a few other sets of skills.<br /> <br /> Now picture him Exalting as a Lunar. Lunar magic follows different paths; he will gain magic flowing from his great strength and toughness, as well as an animal form that's likely thematically connected to his arms-like-iron-bands, and magic related to that (plus the ability to expand into other forms, as well as other aspects of his physical form.) Does this make him a better blacksmith? Well, yes, compared to where he was as a mortal. He can hit the iron harder -- mechanically, he's throwing more dice at the task. And he's a magical being, so he has the basic ability to craft magical things that all magical beings have. (And while I might sound dismissive, both of these are big deals.) But his story as a supernatural being (the epic legend inherent in the Lunar Exaltation that Exalted him) does not care, particularly, that he was using his great strength as a smith or that he honed it as a smith; that's not going to be the direction his charms develop in. Playing this character and expecting to become a legendary smith among the Exalted makes you <a href=\"http://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2006/9/6/\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>, basically -- if you wanted to tell a story about magic flowing through your talent at crafting and enhancing your talent at crafting, why are you playing a type of Exalted that doesn't really work that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-13-2013, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:34:52-08:00","id":10039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes#post9451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals follow visions scoured from the Loom itself to aid in crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally not too fond of this, partially because I can't see many instances where it looks meaningfully different from what a more practically-engaged Exalt would do, and partially because I find ideas of &quot;Sidereals do stuff by seeing the future&quot; to be a really shallow pool to draw ideas from, at least in comparison to their actual published Charmset.<br /> <br /> The idea that they constructed the Jade Prison out of designs they gleaned from patterns in rock formations they were guided to be visions during the Great Prophecy notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not, since I'm now thinking that's what you were probably driving at...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:00:27-08:00","id":10054,"title":"","content":"@ Aquillion:<br /> <br /> You can basiaclly play the game four ways. Combat/Sorcerer/Crafter and Social. We are the worst at sorcery of all Celestial Exalted and the worst of all Exalted at Crafting.<br /> <br /> I'm *not* saying everyone should be able to read fate or shape-shift (not that I would lock players out of stories that lead to such), what I am getting at - is that Lunars are half a splat when you look at them in the light of 2E. Where in 2E it was Full Moon (Str/Dex/Stam) and Pretty Kitty or bust.<br /> <br /> Saying they suck at crafting and sorcery...no shit - No Moons were trash in 2E. I'm saying its about damned time they got something to play with - so they can interact with the other half of the game that they have been locked out of. If it's ***wrong bad fun*** to play a Lunar Crafter - that's what custom charms are for. Also, its the main issue that plagues the Lunar community. The degree of ideas shot down and called out as wrong bad fun on Lunars far outweighs all that heaped upon the rest of the splats combined. If they play that badly with what people want to do and expectations - just brand them with npc and shuck them into the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 11-13-2013, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:14:46-08:00","id":10086,"title":"","content":"I'm imagining a Lunar shaman-savant who weaves sorcery into a magic ring, folding spell after spell into it and twisting up lines of power into the weave. Not sure how it works mechanically, but in my mind, it looks pretty damned cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T19:19:30-08:00","id":10130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10054#post10054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Aquillion: You can basiaclly play the game four ways. Combat/Sorcerer/Crafter and Social. We are the worst at sorcery of all Celestial Exalted and the worst of all Exalted at Crafting..</div> </div> </div> </div> I -think- the core of the point was that being worse than other Exalted and being objectively bad at/unable to do something are not the same thing. As far as the philosophy to the contrary, I chalk it up to my belief that, of all the old White Wolf game lines for which crossover was a sacred cow amongst the player base, for Exalted it was the sacred-est. Most of the other lines have, at least at times, paid lip-service to the idea that crossover, at least rules crossover, is maybe not the best idea. And don't misunderstand-- I like crossover, even when I maybe shouldn't-- but I do think it can sometimes generate a lot of angst for those with a fondness for a particular splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T20:32:18-08:00","id":10165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10054#post10054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Aquillion:<br /> <br /> You can basiaclly play the game four ways. Combat/Sorcerer/Crafter and Social. We are the worst at sorcery of all Celestial Exalted and the worst of all Exalted at Crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are so many things wrong with this I don't even know where to begin.<br /> <br /> First, that division is entirely undesirable. To the extent that it's true (and it isn't -- you completely neglected, for example, the entire Night caste, all non-combat applications of Shapeshifting, etc) -- it's a massive problem that needs to be aggressively fought in the game's design. If the game breaks up neatly into Combat / Sorcerer / Crafter / Social, then all powers and splats are going to become more dull by nature of becoming just yet-another-boring-implementation of the same basic things that that division describes. It also leads to &quot;decker syndrome&quot;, where a character built into one of your rigid divisions becomes useless outside it -- the Combat Guy forced to sit and watch while the Craft Guy crafts; the Sorcerer forced to sit and watch while the Combat Guy fights, etc. These are not desirable things! Sometimes a degree of decker syndrome is inevitable -- it can be hard to fit crafting cleanly into the same paradigm as combat, sure -- but it's not desirable to have rigid divisions like that.<br /> <br /> In any case, it's important that the gameplay be built around thematics rather than forcing thematics to align to some ridiculous rule of gameplay. As a Lunar, you're a master of shapeshifting; your powers are what shapeshifting can do, as well as certain things derived from the thematics of your type of shapeshifting even if they're not the same thing, themselves. Then you find ways of playing the game that explore what this can do. You don't start by saying &quot;well, these are the four ways to play the game, let's make the silver-tinted versions of them.&quot; You find the <i>Lunar</i> was of playing the game (which may not involve, for instance, any sort of crafting, and which may not quite match the Twilight approach to Sorcery), and you develop them into a full splat.<br /> <br /> (What kind of things do you develop, beyond combat and social powers? Well, that's sort of the idea of an entire book, but let's just start with &quot;utility&quot; and go from there. Utility is a lot of things, but the important part from your stiltifyingly rigid breakdown is that they're powers that, among other things, let you bypass combat without having to fight. Transportation and disguise powers are a big part of this, as are senses; some of it can move into more complicated magical effects, which Sorcery <i>has</i> but doesn't have a monopoly on. You blithely described Lunars as the worst Celestial Sorcerers, but the role of &quot;sorcerer&quot; -- to the extent that it's a role -- isn't just about knowing capital-S sorcery, it's the stupifying big role of &quot;everything magical that isn't directly related to one of the other things&quot;; and there's no reason Lunars can't have a lot<br /> <br /> Second, even if it were real, it's irrelevant. The vast majority of Solars, in fact, do not learn Crafting or Solar Circle Sorcery (stereotypically, they fall under one caste!) Obviously Lunars cover less thematic ground than Solars do -- Solars are the core splat, so they're designed to be unusually conceptually broad, to let people play more things without having to buy a splatbook. The individual splats tend to be more narrowly-focused in what you can do with them, catering to a specific taste (but exploring and developing that taste more thoroughly.) In other words, if your options for how you can build a Lunar really did only have the breadth of 4/5th of Solars -- I don't see how that's a problem? Your build is still just your build; just like most Solars never learn Crafting or Solar Circle Sorcery, I don't see how it's a problem to have a splat that never learns crafting or Solar Circle Sorcery. If you want those things, Lunars aren't for you, but -- obviously, there's a ton of players who are perfectly happy with the game without them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying they suck at crafting and sorcery...no shit - No Moons were trash in 2E. I'm saying its about damned time they got something to play with - so they can interact with the other half of the game that they have been locked out of. If it's ***wrong bad fun*** to play a Lunar Crafter - that's what custom charms are for. Also, its the main issue that plagues the Lunar community. The degree of ideas shot down and called out as wrong bad fun on Lunars far outweighs all that heaped upon the rest of the splats combined. If they play that badly with what people want to do and expectations - just brand them with npc and shuck them into the background. </div> </div> </div>The reason why people get that reaction is because they usually look at Lunars, realize they suck, then say <i>GIVE ME ALL THE SOLAR STUFF!</i>, because the Solar stuff is well-developed and it's the only thing they can think of.<br /> <br /> This is a terrible approach to Lunars, because it would make both Lunars and crafting more boring. If your approach to 'fixing' Lunars is to describe the five Solar castes and their approach to the game, then demand that Lunars get all their stuff (roughly -- you completely ignored Nights for inexplicable reasons, combined the Zenith / Eclipse roles into 'social', and listed Twilights twice under Craft / Sorcery; but the basic idea was still 'take the Solar stuff that was elaborated on in the Core, and give it to Lunars), then yeah, your ideas aren't going to help. The trick of fixing Lunars is to find uniquely Lunar stuff to do, not to say &quot;well, what's a Lunar way of approaching the stuff that exists already?&quot; Because we've <i>been</i> there and it was 2e Lunars and it was terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-14-2013, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T20:51:38-08:00","id":10171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet... Lunars make artifacts. They do this, sometimes - or at least they did in 2e.<br /> <br /> However much Lunar artifacture occurs, the rules of the game should be such that it is not implausible that Lunars did it. If Lunars, for example, were canonically responsible for a great host of artifacts, yet their greatest wonderwrights had no more capability at creating artifacts than an exceptionally devoted mortal thaumaturge, that would be confusing and weird. Conversely, if Lunars had canonically never created and meaningful quantity of artifacts, yet they had a host of Charms devoted to the task which were exceptionally capable, that would also be confusing and weird.<br /> <br /> The right hand should not shoot the left hand, that's all I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very few, really. There's a handful of Lunar artifacts and that's it. Compared to the number of artifacts described as being made by Solars or Dragon-Blooded, the Lunar artifacts are almost nonexistent (which is very noticeable when you realize that Lunars have been around for 1500 years and Solars haven't.) Going by WotLA and O's Codex, the artifice of the Twilight caste defined the First Age; the artifice of the Dragon-Blooded defined the Shogunate. Lunar artificers have never defined anything, because (bluntly) Lunars as a group are not good enough or focused enough at making artifacts to ever define an era through artifice.<br /> <br /> That said, as I said in my post -- Lunars are not <i>incapable</i> of making artifacts. They can make artifacts as well as any typical super-strong, super-smart, super-dextrous magical being with a vastly extended lifespan (and, therefore, extended of time periods in which to craft.) That's still pretty good! It's good enough that a Lunar with a bit of time to spare still has a reason to sometimes make something, since there's no sense in wasting that potential; it's good enough that there's no reason for Lunars to neglect the option to do so. If a Lunar wants to devote a lot of time to it, they can even make something pretty impressive.<br /> <br /> It's just that, to them, it's a frivolity -- if you look at the described Lunar artifacts we have, they're almost all objects of sentimental worth, the kind of thing, say, that a swordsman who practices whittling as a hobby might make in his free time, or the kind of thing a deeply-devoted spouse might weave as a present for their lover. These things can still be marvelous to behold! But they're not... a big deal, in the grand scheme of things, and they've never been treated as that. There are Lunars who are capable of crafting if they choose to spend the time to do so, but there are no Lunars whose magic expresses itself, primarily, through their craft, because that's just not how Lunar magic works. There are no Lunars capable of competing with a dedicated Solar or Alchemical artificer, at all. Lunars can be unnaturally fast or strong, and they're magical beings (meaning that they <i>can</i> craft artifacts), and these things together mean that, yeah, some Lunar artifacts exist -- I'd even go far enough to say that a Lunar who lives long enough probably crafts a few things, just because hey, sometimes you need something and if you have the time, it's simpler to do it yourself than to ask someone else -- but...<br /> <br /> None of that requires dedicated crafting charms! In fact, in mechanical terms, none of that requires more than Excellencies. So I don't think Lunars have much, beyond that, that can help with crafting. Maybe a few very general charms that help in an incidental fashion (like a generic speedup charm that enhances all kinds of things a bit, one of which is crafting), but none of what you're describing really requires that Lunars have dedicated crafting magic, and I don't particularly see why they would, so I'm inclined to say... they probably don't. There are craft-focused Solars or Alchemicals who can make magical artifacts staggeringly fast and with blinding ease; there aren't any Lunars who can do that. That doesn't mean that Lunars can't <i>make artifacts</i> -- it means that Lunars make artifacts using the baseline mechanics against which the setting's dedicated artificers look so impressive.<br /> <br /> Which is the heart of the issue. Making anything a generic type of power or focus that every type of Exalted <i>must</i> have ends up stripping it of its meaning. If everyone who wants to make artifiacts can easily get their own version of the Awesome Legendary Artificer suite, then... it doesn't really mean anything to be an Awesome Legendary Artificer, because every single artifact in history will have been made by one. To me, the fact that there are Lunars who made artifacts <i>without</i> something like CNNT or the like is necessary for CNNT and its ilk to mean what they do.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Lunars suck. Their talents are focused in other areas (and if you're a Lunar, you'll have spent your XP in other areas, because... there are no Lunar craft charms.) You'll have other capabilities instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-13-2013, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T21:19:37-08:00","id":10185,"title":"","content":"Christ Aquillion, I've not said to take away from the Solars at all. I'm tired of the personal attacks and tread pooping. You've been reported.<br /> <br /> Just stay out of my threads if all you can do is bash. I welcome the bashing if you provide some alternatives and cool ideas for Lunars. Otherwise, just stay away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T21:54:10-08:00","id":10193,"title":"","content":"As a side-bar, it might be fruitful to drop in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Crafting\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> to the Wiki's dev quotes on Crafting in general in EX3. Makes sense to know the lay of the land. Er, in theory, anyway. Kinda slim pickings on details at the moment, I'm afraid. But here are some that might be worth noting.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: <b>(AlwaysToast)</b><br /> <i>Artifact/Manse creation: When PCs decided to build them. Is building them going to be Fun? Not just picking out the powers, but figuring out how long it will take to build in game. </i><br /> <br /> A: <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Yes. I am very excited about our manses. I am also very fond of point buy systems and crafting/construction, so you should expect a lot of meat from this part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: <b>(BrilliantRain)</b><br /> <i>Will you be able to make cool things with Craft that are not, themselves, Artifacts? </i><br /> <br /> A: <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plague of Hats</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3E the assumed method of artifact crafting is not going to be &quot;2000 x 1010 times longer than crafting a similar mundane item, and the system 'hook' is finding ways to mitigate that bullshit.&quot; If you're absolutely set on just sitting at a forge for ever and ever to create The Bestest Sword +2 that's fine, but that's the &quot;if you don't want to come up with anything interesting and don't want to handwave it either&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I concede I may be reading too much into the first part of that. I'm still hopeful it suggests a typical game might actually see some basic artifact crafting completed without needing to benefit from ALL OF the Solar Craft or something)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> What I'm getting here, the Holden quotes earlier, and a general sense are that Lunars are just plain not gonna get the kinda mileage out of crafting that, say, Solars and Alchemicals are; that in no way stops it from being a fun, meaty, worthwhile pursuit for those who want to explore it. A Lunar who wants to do some crafting will profit from doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:04:35-08:00","id":10205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10054#post10054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Aquillion:<br /> <br /> You can basiaclly play the game four ways. Combat/Sorcerer/Crafter and Social. We are the worst at sorcery of all Celestial Exalted and the worst of all Exalted at Crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, what? Have you <i>looked </i>at the shit a Lunar Sorcerer can pull? Before Glories: Sun introduced Shedding Infinite Radiance, the Lunars had an incredible advantage over everyone else in sorcery due to the No Moon anima power - in fact, while a Solar had the highest ceiling of raw power due to having access to Solar Circle sorcery, a Lunar was<i> better than a Twilight </i>at getting use out of the spell they did have access to. This is because they were the only splat to have gotten an actual metasorcerous effect. Does that sound excessive? That's what a 10m discount on all spells will do for you. Combine it with a Gem of Sorcery or a Key of Mastery for even greater fun! And while sorcerers normally don't get access to their Excellencies to boost their DV while casting, you have a free -1 external penalty on all attacks against you, and your shapeshifting lets you have a Dexterity above 5 for further passive DV-boosting, and, oh, yeah, you can cast while flying.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you're doing all that while under the protection of Phantom Crossfire Feint, because why wouldn't you? And also, while a Solar's mote pool is theoretically higher than yours, you actually have more motes until they start increasing their Virtues, and even when they outpace you you still spent comparatively less xp on the same Essence, and given how mote-expensive sorcery is... And Sidereals, the only other Celestial Circle sorcerers? They're <i>in the dust.</i><br /> <br /> So, yeah. Lunars: they make battle-sorcery an actually plausible prospect in 2.5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:38:05-08:00","id":10222,"title":"","content":"Perhaps significant story events related to the subjects of their personal Intimacies prompt them to cry out precious stones like the Samebito, or in a more general sense, produce important raw materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:38:58-08:00","id":10224,"title":"","content":"I maintain Lunars are MacGuyvering mystics whose crafts are multi-purpose. Solars are the perfect crafters, but they aren't the most &quot;creative&quot;. The Solar will create the best daiklave or firewand. The Lunar will create the Firewand-klaive. A Solar does not tarry himself with imperfect materials for his creations. Only the purest samples will do. A Lunar can hackjob a few busted things together and make a ramshackle artifact that will suit him for a short time. Also let's not oust Lunar crafting just yet. There is such a thing called The Caul, which is both crafted by Lunars, and is a goddamn island that's got its own Loom effect AKA Fate. Make of that what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T23:29:56-08:00","id":10239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10185#post10185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christ Aquillion, I've not said to take away from the Solars at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, you described (most of) the main areas of Solar expertise as if they were the areas of &quot;general&quot; mechanics which all Exalted get. None of them are unique to Solars, but if you make them all generic to the point where everyone gets all of them, you're making Solars entirely generic (as well as, well, almost everyone else), even if you don't realize it. I feel that making something like crafting into just a generic mechanic that everyone has their own implementation of takes away from its meaning.<br /> <br /> Which is what I was getting at when I compared giving everyone, without exception, access to Craft charms regardless of theme, to giving everyone, without exception, access to shapeshifting regardless of theme. There are non-Lunar shapeshifting powers where it's thematically appropriate, (Sidereals can turn into a raven; Infernals have all their wacky madness), but if you make shapeshifting into just something everyone does in their own way, then I feel you take away from the significance of Lunars being the legendary shapeshifting splat.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if everyone gets craft charms regardless of how well it fits into their themes, then it no longer means as much for Twilights to have forged the wonders of the First Age, or for Alchemicals to be the Chosen of the Great Maker. I don't feel that sacrificing these things is worth the dubious benefit of giving Lunars some shoehorned-in Craft charms, because I don't think that crafting is ever going to be particularly important to what Lunars are or to the overall experience of playing a Lunar.<br /> <br /> If you feel that this leaves a hole in No Moon competence, why not focus on other things to fill it in? I guess my real question is -- what do you <i>want</i> for Lunars, that you feel only crafting can provide? What are you trying to accomplish here that makes it necessary for them to have crafting charms? It feels like you can't really picture Lunar crafting charms either -- like you said, permanence and leaving a lasting mark on the world are not huge deals for Lunars, although they probably have ways to do it.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not just trying to be obstinate -- I think that there are real, significant problems with giving Lunars anything that's clearly &quot;craft-themed&quot;, at least if it's being done just for the sake of making sure they have Crafting Powers; and I particularly object to the idea of giving Lunar craft effects just because everyone should have craft effects. If your issue is that you feel that No Moons need some sort of special magic of their own, I think it would be cool, but the whole idea of making it something of their own would be to get away from the existing magics of Sorcery and Crafting. In general, I think most of the &quot;uniquely Lunar&quot; No Moon magic is therefore likely to involve making particular alterations to their body or making things out of parts of their body -- growing enchanted gemstones in their palms or forehead, etc, as a part of them or an extension of themselves rather than crafting separate artifacts. One of Monkey's tricks was to pull hairs from his tail and turn them into things; that, say, seems like a uniquely Lunar magic.<br /> <br /> But the underlying problem is that there isn't yet a coherent theme to Lunar magic that could illuminate ideas like those beyond the very basic, core shapeshifting stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-14-2013, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:25:26-08:00","id":10260,"title":"","content":"I think the Caul is supposed to have some Artifact to take over the functions of the Loom of Fate?<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that Lunar<i>s</i> are capable of such mighty feats of artifice, but that <i>a</i> Lunar occasionally does.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the actual setting and gameplay, concrete achievements have more worth than abstract power ceilings.<br /> <br /> Lunars probably don't have a general defining paradigm of crafting, or a collective cultural contribution to it, but that doesn't mean that no Lunar ever crafted something important.<br /> <br /> It's the same basic logic as the Scarlet Empress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:47:20-08:00","id":10269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10171#post10171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very, very few, really. There's a handful of Lunar artifacts and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overlooking how 2nd edition handled the Moonsilver tattoos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T02:21:27-08:00","id":10281,"title":"","content":"There is or shouldn't be anything that prevents a Lunar from being a master craftsman. Using the trickster archetype Coyote sung the world into being. The metal workers of Africa are/were all said to be able to become hyenas. I'm certain I could find more examples if I tried As I recall working with moon silver was said to be partly a religious experience and Lunar were loathe to allow Solar access. Should Lunar equal Solar and the related Infernal and Abyssal probably not except when it comes to working with moon silver then I'd say yes they should equal Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:48:59-08:00","id":10305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10281#post10281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall working with moon silver was said to be partly a religious experience and Lunar were loathe to allow Solar access.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a good idea to perpetuate elements of hostility and competition between Lunars and Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incbill</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunar equal Solar and the related Infernal and Abyssal probably not except when it comes to working with moon silver then I'd say yes they should equal Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that manifest beyond really weird Charms like &quot;exactly like Solar Craft Charm, but only works for moonsilver&quot;?<br /> <br /> Lunars probably have a strong affinity for moonsilver, since it can do a lot of things that fit them well, but I don't think it's useful to define that in terms of an equality in crafting with Solars.<br /> <br /> When it comes to overall crafting, if it's going to be a priority, I'd say it's more useful for the way Lunars do it to have a distinctive character than to cover some method that nobody else can use or some specific material that they're really good at crafting.<br /> <br /> Although mostly, I'm having a hard time seeing it as a priority. I kind of expect that a Lunar who wants to craft Artifacts is mostly using their dice pools, and the occasional Charm that can have some utility in crafting without being part of a cascade of craft Charms meant to imply that it's a thing with them.<br /> <br /> I think there are places where people need to see characters who do things without being an Exalt of doing that thing. There's a system there underneath the Charms, and I hope and expect that it will shine in its own right.<br /> <br /> This seems especially pertinent to Lunars, with their Attribute Charms and things the developers have said concerning them not really being a function-oriented Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:15:38-08:00","id":10314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10239#post10239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean is, you described (most of) the main areas of Solar expertise as if they were the areas of &quot;general&quot; mechanics which all Exalted get. None of them are unique to Solars, but if you make them all generic to the point where everyone gets all of them, you're making Solars entirely generic (as well as, well, almost everyone else), even if you don't realize it. I feel that making something like crafting into just a generic mechanic that everyone has their own implementation of takes away from its meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crafting is not something created for Solars though. It is something that humanity - without an Exaltation, is meant to favor. Autochthon favored man kind because they had a built in (genetic/designed) deposition for the use of faith, dogma and tools. Craft is based on tools and the Alchemicals book even says that humans in Autochthon are often the greatest craftsmen.<br /> <br /> It is the inheritance of humanity to be craftsmen - or so the lore claims. It is humanities distinction from the beasts that we build infrastructure and use tools. All Exalts come from human stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 11-14-2013, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:38:52-08:00","id":10324,"title":"","content":"Actually I don't particularly care if the innate hostility between Lunar and Solars disappears. What I was trying to do was explain that there maybe times when a Lunar could equal a Solar at crafting. A Solar for instance without charms would be at a serious disadvantage crafting a daiklaive vs a Lunar who shapes his hand into an hammer his legs unto an anvil and uses a portable forge to heat the iron,etc. While pounding the mixture into a daiklaive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:53:19-08:00","id":10330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10314#post10314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the inheritance of humanity to be craftsmen - or so the lore claims. It is humanities distinction from the beasts that we build infrastructure and use tools. All Exalts come from human stock.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why doesn't that mean you can have a Lunar crafter who does it without Charms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10324#post10324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was trying to do was explain that there maybe times when a Lunar could equal a Solar at crafting. A Solar for instance without charms would be at a serious disadvantage crafting a daiklaive vs a Lunar who shapes his hand into an hammer his legs unto an anvil and uses a portable forge to heat the iron,etc. While pounding the mixture into a daiklaive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not really proving anything when you're comparing a Solar without Charms to another Exalt with Charms.<br /> <br /> And the specific example of a Lunar who turns their hand into a hammer and their legs(?) into an anvil just feels... really weird.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters, but that doesn't mean that there aren't things that people feel like they're really reaching for wanting them to be able to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T05:05:35-08:00","id":10334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10330#post10330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why doesn't that mean you can have a Lunar crafter who does it without Charms?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're not really proving anything when you're comparing a Solar without Charms to another Exalt with Charms.<br /> <br /> And the specific example of a Lunar who turns their hand into a hammer and their legs(?) into an anvil just feels... really weird.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters, but that doesn't mean that there aren't things that people feel like they're really reaching for wanting them to be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCan't hold it against Incbill too much - there is little revealed as to how most Lunar charms will work. In this time of flux I expect most iterations of ideas to be a tad odd or resonate strangely.<br /> <br /> In regards to Lunar Crafter without charms? Well your going to have your excellency either way. When you look at crafting it is the *only* ability that is ***three attributes*** + 1 ability. So sure, if Lunars can use all three excellencies to boost perception/Int and Dex that works. It is also for this same reason that one could argue Attribute splats should be the best at crafting @_@<br /> <br /> Sol is no great craftmen, the dragons are no great craftsmen, Luna might well be a great craftsmen in one of the thosand faces she wears - it hardly matters. If I were to put the Exalted in order on crafting I would do it thus:<br /> <br /> Infernals//Solars&lt;-(different fields)-&gt;Lunars//Alchemicals//Sidereals//Dragonbloods//Abyssals<br /> <br /> Granted they could all do it - simply in very differnt ways. I feel Alchemicals give up too much of their humanity (clarity) to even be creative craftsmen. Of them all I could see them being the fastest but far from the most skilled. Lunars are all about vision, creativity and adaptability - they would make great artists at the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T05:37:47-08:00","id":10342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10023#post10023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting is also one of &quot;the different mechanics of the game!&quot; If you believe that all Exalted should have paths to all the different mechanics of the game, then you also believe that the game needs a Solar take on shapeshifting or a Dragon-Blooded take on weaving Fate.<br /> <br /> Lunars may have some charms that incidentally help them at crafting, but I don't think that there should be any &quot;Lunar craft charms&quot; -- attempts to shoehorn them in in previous editions have been part of the thinking that led to the bland sameness that infected so much of the 2e Lunar charmset. Different charmsets follow different types of logic; the logic of Lunar magic doesn't (or shouldn't) focus on those kinds of competencies or skills in the way that, say, Solar or Lunar magic does.<br /> <br /> It isn't something that any Lunar fan should <i>want</i> wordcount wasted on in the Lunars book. If you line up the Exalted we know about according to how close crafting fits into their thematics, Lunars are -- literally, no question -- at the very bottom of the list. Solars, Sidereals, DBs, Abyssals, and, in 3e, Infernals are all Ability-based to some extent or another and therefore have a dedicated Craft tree; Solars are explicitly based on skill and human endeavor to an extent, while Abyssals and Infernals are altered Solar shards; Infernals inherit the powers of the makers of the universe; Alchemicals are Attribute-based, but are the chosen of the Great Maker.<br /> <br /> Lunars have nothing. Luna is not a famous crafter, and their charmset is not structured in a way that leads to any particular focus on crafting themes. The reason you can't think of how Lunar craft could work is because it doesn't really fit into their themes at all. Sure, you could force the issue and give Lunars crappy bottom-rung dedicated crafting powers that are, no question, strictly worse than everyone else's (because, again, everyone else has at least some route to crafting in their themes, and Lunars do not), but <i>why</i>? Why do you want that? People happily make numerous Solars who never learn to Craft, and DBs who never learn to craft, and Sidereals and Infernals and Abyssals and Alchemicals who never learn to craft. I don't understand why some Lunar fans feel that access to crafting is important. Nothing in Lunar themes or concepts makes it particularly relevant to being a Lunar; nothing inherent in the Exalted requires that you have access to it (because, again, people happily play numerous Exalted of the other types who never learn it -- in fact, I would say the vast majority of Exalted never learn to craft, even among types like Solars and Alchemicals where the potential is a big deal.)<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Lunar manual should contain a single specific 'crafting charm'; I don't see how it benefits Lunars to include it. Devote the wordcount to something (anything!) else, to developing some other aspect of Lunar power that actually fits their core themes rather than trying to mindlessly ape the themes that were appropriate for other types of Exalted. The different splats are meant to be fundimentally distinct -- they support different types of stories and are focused in different areas. Some of this includes growing in directions or ways that other splats don't; some of this includes, yeah, lacking magical access to areas of expertise and types of charms that other splats have.<br /> <br /> ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So...ah...I've actually managed to make at least one (in fact a few more, even, although the other one isn't strictly crafting so much as it is getting more out of an already crafted item) that I tend to think is uniquely Lunar in nature. It's below:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1715991\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.white-wolf.com/default...osts&amp;m=1715991</a><br /> <br /> And I tend to think that the reason why people can't think of how Lunar craft would work is because the only &quot;way craft would work&quot; that is really visible in people's minds is Solar Craft, and so everyone keeps thinking of it in terms of giving them the Charms Solars have for it. If you actually tried to make it &quot;non-Solar&quot;, than you could easily come up with a Lunar craft that's all its own.<br /> <br /> I mean frankly, Sidereals and Abyssals are the ones that I can't understand the crafting ability of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":781,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","user":"Chained Divinity","date":". 11-14-2013, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T05:50:42-08:00","id":10351,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lunars did not accomplish this kind of thing after the Usurpation (in previous editions), ergo, they don't have the capability to do so meaningfully&quot; can be applied to so many areas of expertise that you could use it to justify the removal of a large chunk of the domain of Exalted mechanics from Lunar capability. It's also a specious argument, as Sidereals have accomplished little of note by making Artifacts while having a decent Crafting suite.<br /> <br /> I should also point out that the rest of the Exalted have Charms to deal with all Abilities--where they don't (e.g., Infernals and War) it was due to lack of space rather than thematic reasons. All the other Exalted have Crafting Charms, but if Lunars got them it would make everyone else generic?<br /> <br /> I should <i>also</i> point out that Shapeshifting is, like manipulating fate or making things out of solid light, a means to do things. Saying &quot;Lunars lack the capability to do all these things, but they can shapeshift!&quot; is not a meaningful trade-off. Sure, turning into a cat is neat, but at the end of the day it's either useful or it isn't: it either has a measurable mechanical impact (in stealth, in damage, in flight, etc.) or it doesn't. And I'm sure you'll find that shapeshifting can, one way or another, be used to make things.<br /> <br /> As an addendum to the above, &quot;utility&quot; is something that everyone gets. Let's look at Sidereals! The ability to bypass combat without having to fight? No one else does it better: not only are they masters of disguise in a way that fools even supernatural senses, they are also the best at saying &quot;no, I don't feel like fighting today&quot; and avoiding encounters altogether. Transportation and disguise powers? They have excellent travelling Charms as well as access to Yu-Shan gates: Sidereals may be the most mobile Exalted of all! And their disguise powers are, as previously mentioned, excellent. If you even want to pretend that they're in the same class under your idea, you'd have to show how they get a similar amount of cool in their budget: assume they're both equally capable at everything, then justify each departure by showing something neat that they gain in exchange.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Lunars deserve billing as Celestial Exalted under your vision. They haven't done much, they have entire areas of competence that they're not supposed to shine at, and at best they're going to match other Celestials in the things they do excel at. They would work better as a (narratively) minor type of Exalt, like the Liminal. This might even be a better way to deal with the idea of &quot;the Werewolf Exalted&quot;, but unfortunately that's not what they're being billed as for Exalted 3. If you avertise them as a Celestial Exalt that is close in power to Solars and about even with Sidereals, people will be justified in expecting them to perform on par with the other two at anything they care to make a character about.<br /> <br /> Finally, I don't find a blanket &quot;no&quot; to be as interesting as an intelligent &quot;yes, but&quot; or &quot;yes, and&quot;. A solution in which Lunars excel at making particular things or at making things with quirks will allow for more character options and be a much stronger statement about Lunars than a simple &quot;they can't do this&quot; (a requirement of years, decades or centuries to make things is equivalent to &quot;can't do this&quot; for players, whom the rules are meant for). Gunnerkrigg Court's Coyote messing up the different tasks he takes out of boredom (e.g., sorting the stars into constellations) or distraction (e.g., sneezing when creating people) and then all of his &quot;gifts&quot; having serious flaws that threaten the user's health or sanity (e.g., the debilitating tree-body for Ysengrin, the host body-killing possession eyes for Renard) are fascinating material--surely this kind of thing is in theme for the tricksters among the Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","user":"Black Paper Moon","date":". 11-14-2013, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:25:37-08:00","id":10390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10351#post10351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should <i>also</i> point out that Shapeshifting is, like manipulating fate or making things out of solid light, a means to do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulating fate might be even narrower than shapeshifting, and Solars don't do very much with solid light.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying &quot;Lunars lack the capability to do all these things, but they can shapeshift!&quot; is not a meaningful trade-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't care about trade-offs so much as focus and expression of source materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, turning into a cat is neat, but at the end of the day it's either useful or it isn't: it either has a measurable mechanical impact (in stealth, in damage, in flight, etc.) or it doesn't. And I'm sure you'll find that shapeshifting can, one way or another, be used to make things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but that doesn't necessarily mean they're especially notable at making things compared to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Lunars deserve billing as Celestial Exalted under your vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are you talking to...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you avertise them as a Celestial Exalt that is close in power to Solars and about even with Sidereals, people will be justified in expecting them to perform on par with the other two at anything they care to make a character about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals and Solars are already very different to one another, so the standards for Lunars that assume there has to be some kind of generic competency for all three of them has always been weird.<br /> <br /> I think Lunars should come across as worthy of the god portrayed in Glories of the Most High, and that will be enough. And Luna managed to have credibility alongside the other Incarnae without arbitrarily latching on parity (up to and including the fact that the Unconquered Sun and the Maidens have things related to crafting in their Panoplies and Luna does not).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:50:40-08:00","id":10407,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Okay, the discussion about if Lunars <i>should</i> have charms to aid in crafting needs to be taken elsewhere. The &quot;no thread crapping&quot; rules still apply. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:07:37-08:00","id":10412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10390#post10390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manipulating fate might be even narrower than shapeshifting, and Solars don't do very much with solid light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulating fate is significantly broader than shapeshifting, actually, at least given the narrowing down of it you've expressed (no growing extra brains, no hammers-for-hands), because you could apply it to a great many situations--getting rid of all that waste energy that's a problem in making things, removing the off-chances that bad things happen that creates issues with making certain things, deciding you weren't there when a blow happened, making someone more inclined to listen to you...shapeshifting, meanwhile, is physical stuff and disguise material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I don't care about trade-offs so much as focus and expression of source materials. </div> </div> </div>What would you define as Lunar source material?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, but that doesn't necessarily mean they're especially notable at making things compared to others. </div> </div> </div>Having their own style of making things=/=being especially notable for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sidereals and Solars are already very different to one another, so the standards for Lunars that assume there has to be some kind of generic competency for all three of them has always been weird. </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be generic competency, it would be a particular brand of competency addressing a major facet of changing the world. You can actually do that with Lunars and crafting, despite assertions to the contrary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Lunars should come across as worthy of the god portrayed in Glories of the Most High, and that will be enough. And Luna managed to have credibility alongside the other Incarnae without arbitrarily latching on parity (up to and including the fact that the Unconquered Sun and the Maidens have things related to crafting in their Panoplies and Luna does not). </div> </div> </div>It isn't really a matter of parity in this case, again. It's a matter of making available character concepts that actually fit more with Lunars than (say) Solars but can also do the crafting thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:12:29-08:00","id":10474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes#post9451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a bridge to 3E for Lunars (which is looking to be 2-3 years out from the time I write this) what *are* the themes of Lunars? I've become so lost over the course of 2E.<br /> <br /> I feel each Exalt should have a path to the different mechanics of the game. Sidereals follow visions scoured from the Loom itself to aid in crafting. Dragon Bloods are able to create great wonders that resonate with their elemental property. I could think of several charms for each of those splats....<br /> <br /> However, when I come to Lunars, I am lost. Making things is about permanance, a lasting mark. This can match up with the survival and warden themes to a degree...but the mecurial and ever changing nature of the Moonkin not so much. Appealing to the Wyld themes - I feel that both 3E is going to abandon them to the Fay and that it does not lend itself well to direct crafting (vision quest to your hearts content). Lunars are neither the Animal Exalted nor would those themes aid in any way. Autochthon choose man because of their capability for Faith, Dogma, and *Tools*. Animals had no tools and pretty much suck at building things compared to man kind.<br /> <br /> I don't even feel I grasp the theme of the Lunar any more. All we know thus far is Rage? That they can shapeshift? These are not themes - at least ones that I could adapt to the mechanics of Sorcery, Crafting, or most (but not all) social interactions?<br /> <br /> I'm just curious and a bit flustered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as an Attribute Exalt, their area of expertise is a blanket over all the abilities, rather than the specific skills of each ability in question... so I think they'll be just as good at Craft as anything else. Because they favor the Attribute, they're going to be just as good at Ripping and Tearing things apart as they (potentially) could be at building and designing.<br /> <br /> This doesn't make them the least capable crafters among the Exalts by any means, its just a different avenue for them to take to reach the exact same end. (I'm not talking about tiering powers between exalts..more like a power range they all fit into).<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting, as has been mentioned earlier, can be an extreme help. Shifting into smaller forms to better build tiny clockwork, and into bigger and stronger ones to heft heavy objects...and into tentacley ones to hold multiple parts at once. They can really make some strange and exotic artifacts like this, and not to mention if they have rare forms for magical ingredients they could potentially already have acquired, say, the spit of Furnace Rhino or the quills of (insert animal).<br /> <br /> And Rage...well... I for one can imagine someone so pissed off they refuse to quit until they figure it out. And then the hundreds pound sword comes crashing through the wall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ehh...I just don't see that they would be particularly bad at crafting, in 3e, if they're just as good in all Attributes. They may or may not have a 'crafting' tree, but then, they won't have a 'melee' tree. That's focusing on abilities. Unfortunately, I can't currently think of an acceptable alternative, but I haven't been thinking on it over a year or two as the developers have. I say trust that they'll give you something awesome. You can't really do much else anyway. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:57:48-08:00","id":10571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10474#post10474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as an Attribute Exalt, their area of expertise is a blanket over all the abilities, rather than the specific skills of each ability in question... so I think they'll be just as good at Craft as anything else. Because they favor the Attribute, they're going to be just as good at Ripping and Tearing things apart as they (potentially) could be at building and designing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that Attributes aren't the only factor to consider here. Lunars aren't Solars-that-are-less-good-but-just-as-broad-everywhere: Lunars have particular themes of their own, and <i>those</i> may not lend themselves to Crafting so much. This isn't really something that's being debated, outside &quot;should things be this way:&quot; the devs have indicated that no, Lunar magic doesn't really work to make them exceptional crafters among the Exalted Host. This is not the same as saying they don't get stuff that a crafter would find useful -- there have been suggestions for creating raw materials that other crafters might find a huge pain to obtain, growing multiple arms that give all the benefits of multiple arms some of which are helpful to Crafters (counting as an equally skilled assistant, perhaps?).<br /> <br /> I think part of people seeing this as a huge problem is the way 2e handled crafting (which is true of many things): outside of Charms, there wasn't much of a system to it, so if you didn't have Charms specifically for crafting, you were out of luck. If the system is robust -- and hatewheel's said he intends it to be meaty -- there may well be enough hooks for thematically Lunar stuff to be of use. Just, again, Lunars as crafters isn't really the big point of emphasis.<br /> <br /> Another thing that might help is getting some more examples of stuff EX3 Lunars actually do. So, okay, their Attribute Charms don't have stuff geared around crafting. What are their Attribute Charms geared around doing/being? Particularly their mental Attribute Charms; if the Caste Attributes are still broken down by physical, social, and mental (this may not be a viable assumption), it would be mystifying to pick a theme that leaves 1/3 of their Castes in the lurch again. Seeing awesome, substantive places this wordcount might wind up going would take out the sting. ... This is also probably better suited for that thread I made and complained about seeing derailed, so I'mma stop helping this derail and get back on topic. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Holden mentioned in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9902#post9902\">the quotes I posted</a> that Lunar craftsmanship will typically take the form of some piece of personal kit for himself or another. That's mainly a lead-in, and certainly not an affirmation that Lunars are in any way gifted at making stuff for themselves and particular individuals. To take it that way would completely blow off all the context around it. Still, it sounds like a cool idea, so I'm running with it as a fun direction anyway: perhaps they do have Charms that are good at making things, but things with a personal bent, i.e. stuff meant for their use, for the use of someone they care about, or for use <i>against/for</i> someone they care about. It would tie into Luna's stronger connection to Intimacies/Ties than to Motivation/Principles. This could fit into the physicality trends of the Charmset by requiring that the Lunar include something of the individual (blood's likely) in the construction. Doing so may create a daiklave that's decent enough on its own, but allows (much easier?) access to particular evocations when used for or against a particular person. Or possibly someone sufficiently related, e.g. a wife or daughter may find the family daiklave just as helpful as the father, while such a weapon meant to oppose one Dynast may be <i>quite good </i>at cutting off a whole branch of the family tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:39:51-08:00","id":10611,"title":"","content":"I'd say there are two places where Lunar &quot;Craft&quot; can fit in.<br /> <br /> First is the idea of transforming your body so that it can aquire the functionality of even the most complex tools- artifacts. Turning your arms to hammers and legs into an anvil isn't very Lunarish. However, eating raw materials and regurgitating a complete artifact? That's brushing against the wall of weirdness that Lunars maybe shouldn't be on the other side of, but still is something I find cool and very Lunar. Or, say, a charm that lets you eat one type of a material and through your supernatural metabolism transform it into moonsilver. Or, I can see a charm that lets you shed your skin like a snake and use it as a special material to craft a very resilent armour. Or maybe creating heartstones in your belly like kideny-stones. That's ugly, that's distasteful, that's animalistic.<br /> <br /> The other is the idea of incorporating artifacts into your body. How about a charm that allows you to devour artifacts and gain their powers, as a part of your body? Or an ability to fuse your body with a physical object? Sticking artifacts into your body and hiding them the way Solars hide them in Elsewhere, only more visceral? Hell, you could turn into a real armadillo of daiklaves sticking out of your body. That could be cool.<br /> <br /> Of course, magical tattos also fall under this. I'd even go as far as to say that maybe not only should Lunars excel at crafting moonsilver tattos, but it should something completely exclusive to them. Or at the very least be treated the same way crafting normal artifacts is treated for Lunars- they can do it, but don't have charms helping in it. Even though it's much more narrow than normal artifice, it could very well be &quot;stuff that only Lunars have officaly published charms to hellp with&quot;. How cool would be a chain of charms that allow you to create more and more potent tattos of moonsilver? Maybe you could have charms that unlock evocations for moonsilver tattos you wouldn't otherwise be able to obtain with more &quot;external&quot; artifice? There is a rich mine of ideas here.<br /> <br /> Note that I do not expect any of these ideas expanded upon in the official material. I would, however, greatly appreciate a solid benchmark that would allow me to turn them into custom charms &lt;wink, wink&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-14-2013, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:02:57-08:00","id":10711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10611#post10611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe creating heartstones in your belly like kideny-stones. That's ugly, that's distasteful, that's animalistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are &quot;ugly&quot; or &quot;distasteful&quot; going to be descriptive of Lunar magic? I think that sort of organic squick is being concentrated into the Liminal Exalted -- reanimated corpses with Aspects based on substances like blood and soil -- and out of the Lunar Exalted, whose social magic provides &quot;majestic, glorious god-bodies&quot;. Are barbarian beast-gods supposed to be hideous and icky or awe-inspiringly beautiful?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, what crafting-related Second Edition Lunar Charms do you think will return, or not?<br /> <br /> <br /> Flaw-Finding Examination sadly shared a name with a Dragon-Blooded Charm -- and was even so self-aware as to admit it -- but the idea was sound. It's a Perception Charm where the Lunar determines an object's weakest point, and therefore how best to break it. By turning that understanding around, a Lunar can identify how an object is broken, which hastens the task of fixing it.<br /> <br /> There was no Dexterity or Wits Charm to hasten dramatic-time-scale actions so that a Lunar could repair or make things faster (which could be applied to administering medical aid, studying and researching, traveling, or any other form of manual labor), but there could have been. Certainly, Alchemicals got one, and I'm not talking about Creator Fugue Engine. I think it was Inexplicable Efficiency Upgrade.<br /> <br /> Luna's Blessed Hands was rather uninspired and unimpressive. It was just a much worse knock-off of a Solar Charm, where the Solar Charm covered all forms of crafting and the Lunar version only covered moonsilver -- while neglecting Lunar-aspected manses. At the very least, LBH could have upgraded Clay-Wetting Practice or something, seeing as that Charm was forbidden from targeting magical materials.<br /> <br /> Clay-Wetting Practice and Weapon Shaping Method... well, I have no idea. Are Lunars going to focus entirely on transforming themselves rather than their surroundings? Are they still supposed to be highly adaptable?<br /> <br /> I'm betting that Lunar Blade Reconfiguration will NOT return. That seems like the sort of thing Evocations ought to do. Makes it simpler to justify why LBR only seems designed to work with weapons (since it will be a weapon's Evocation) but doesn't really do anything with other moonsilver objects like armor. Likewise, we might see the return of First Edition's Surprising Moonsilver Deformation and Insidious Moonsilver Shard as Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the other First Edition Lunar Charms was an homage to a Classic WoD werewolf Gift, Shaping The Once-Living Form. This Gift or Charm made it much easier to fashion clothing, tools and weapons out of fur, horns, bone, shells, wood, etc. Very &quot;barbaric&quot;, though much more limited than Clay-Wetting Practice, which did basically the same thing, but with any inorganic material as well.<br /> <br /> Well, maybe Clay-Wetting Practice could be an upgrade to Shaping the Once-Living Form, so that the Lunar learns to progress from wood to steel?<br /> <br /> But all of this is moot if the Lunars cannot transform anything but themselves. Of course, if they can't do that, they can't curse others with the forms of beasts or others, as with Wondrous Lunar Transformation.<br /> <br /> And would Lunars NOT have the ability to make men into women and humans into animals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:50:22-08:00","id":10741,"title":"","content":"Items that shapeshift? Here's my moonsilver quill pen/Daiklave/tipped talons.<br /> <br /> Shamanistic fetishes? Not sure where I'd go from that thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:03:22-08:00","id":10754,"title":"","content":"I think a big problem with this discussion is that we don't really know how Craft is supposed to work in 3E. I mean, in 2E, effective Craft Charms were basically limited to penalty negators and speed enhancers, with cap breakers like Wonder-Forging Genius in the high Essence part of the game. That's... not a lot to work from as a basis for design, no matter how creative you are.<br /> <br /> What it comes down to is where the &quot;hooks&quot; for the Craft system are in 3E. What, exactly, can we do with Craft as a mundane Ability, and how do we do the breakdown between short-term or smaller projects (like cooking or sewing a shirt), longer-term or bigger projects (like building a house or a warstrider) and the <i>really</i> big stuff (artifacts, manses, and stuff on the scale of the Penitent of the Lap)? We need to know the answers to these questions before we try to make any statements about what kind of Charms Lunars should have.<br /> <br /> Based on what the devs have said, it would seem to mean that Lunars will be able to quickly and efficiently set up temporary structures like war camps or impromptu shelters, while having more difficulty with the kinds of projects we normally associate with artifice. On the one hand, they don't rely on massive infrastructure or extended supply lines for their efforts, but on the other hand, projects that absolutely require such things are outside the reach of their magic. Don't know how this will play out in the system itself, but I'm sure it'd be interesting to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:10:33-08:00","id":10767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10711#post10711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are &quot;ugly&quot; or &quot;distasteful&quot; going to be descriptive of Lunar magic? I think that sort of organic squick is being concentrated into the Liminal Exalted -- reanimated corpses with Aspects based on substances like blood and soil -- and out of the Lunar Exalted, whose social magic provides &quot;majestic, glorious god-bodies&quot;. Are barbarian beast-gods supposed to be hideous and icky or awe-inspiringly beautiful?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Majestic god bodies&quot; is the only real description we've had so far. I suspect Lunar magic <i>can</i> be ugly or distasteful -- killing to take a form still seems to be the default (and may remain as heart-tasting), and I imagine the... &quot;traditional&quot; route to beastmen is still go (the existence of alternatives has been confirmed for the former, and I will be pleased if the latter gets some, too). I imagine it might be something the Lunar decides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, what crafting-related Second Edition Lunar Charms do you think will return, or not? </div> </div> </div>Good run-down!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But all of this is moot if the Lunars cannot transform anything but themselves. Of course, if they can't do that, they can't curse others with the forms of beasts or others, as with Wondrous Lunar Transformation.<br /> <br /> And would Lunars NOT have the ability to make men into women and humans into animals? </div> </div> </div>Confirmation would make me incredibly happy. Minimal shaping of the world around them can be fine, but stuff like Wondrous/Insidious Luna Transformation (hopefully new things, maybe to the tune of infectious lycanthropy?) feel like it's right in their mythic wheelhouse. Leaving it out would feel like a huge missed opportunity, and I'd be deeply curious about what the devs feel would justify that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T16:18:29-08:00","id":10880,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10039#post10039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally not too fond of this, partially because I can't see many instances where it looks meaningfully different from what a more practically-engaged Exalt would do, and partially because I find ideas of &quot;Sidereals do stuff by seeing the future&quot; to be a really shallow pool to draw ideas from, at least in comparison to their actual published Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeah, Sidereal magic is surprisingly not *just* about seeing the future. <br /> <br /> Now, when people play Sidereals, they play them for characters who can see the future. And that's a big part of their appeal, being visionary. <br /> <br /> And they do actually have a lot of Charms that do work on this basis, seeing the weave of events and using this information to avoid problems, find the best solution, etc. They have a lot of powers like this in the &quot;knowing&quot; abilities (awareness, lore, Funnily enough it seems like seeing the future shows up most in their combat Charms - Jedi warriors are cool!<br /> <br /> Still, seeing the future, is far from the sole expression of how their Charms work. They're not simple precognitives. Their Charms tend to at least as much and probably more be about manipulating and declaring fate, according to their own passions and vision - exchanging fates, drawing auspicious and useful fates and their essences to themselves, dealing with spirits and making bargains (with fate and spirits), etc. with little actual basis in trying to see what the future is *supposed* to be. Actually a lot of people find these to be the more evocative and attention grabbing parts of their Charmset (but again, they're not the only part and Sidereals without that visionary aspect would be missing something).<br /> <br /> There's room in their craft magic for both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10571#post10571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden mentioned in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=9902#post9902\">the quotes I posted</a> that Lunar craftsmanship will typically take the form of some piece of personal kit for himself or another. That's mainly a lead-in, and certainly not an affirmation that Lunars are in any way gifted at making stuff for themselves and particular individuals. To take it that way would completely blow off all the context around it. Still, it sounds like a cool idea, so I'm running with it as a fun direction anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at those quotes, they seem to boil down to -<br /> <br /> 1. Shapeshifting generally doesn't help with crafting. (this is not a ban on shapeshifting magic that does, just a statement)<br /> 2. Intelligence Charms, on the other hand, clearly can. (although from context and what else the writers have said these will have to not take the form of &quot;giant brain&quot; Charms).<br /> 3. Lunars don't tend towards large scale &quot;engineering&quot; projects because their current style (and perhaps this is a bit of a product of a persisting nature) trends them towards being on the run, travelling light and high mobility, &quot;off the grid&quot;.<br /> 4. This said, Lunars don't necessarily make quite as much personal gear for themselves either, because of higher tool independence (just notably more than large scale projects).<br /> 5. They clearly aren't going to outperform Solars at any kind of crafting, even if they wanted to focus the same way, which they wouldn't for reasons. This is not to say that they are bad - they are very good, just that Solars are better at it.<br /> <br /> Hard to argue with any of that. Phrasing Lunar crafting in terms of the restrictions from their present situation and their strengths making certain kinds of gear unnecessary is a lot more useful than saying that it would take away from other splats to have them be good at certain abilities (or Attribute magic doesn't support crafting like it does combat etc.).<br /> <br /> I like the ideas ITT about Lunar crafting power involving personal, authentic, uncontrolled passion and organic qualities (e.g. Gaius's post).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:23:50-08:00","id":11191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10880#post10880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at those quotes, they seem to boil down to -<br /> <br /> 1. Shapeshifting generally doesn't help with crafting. (this is not a ban on shapeshifting magic that does, just a statement)<br /> 2. Intelligence Charms, on the other hand, clearly can. (although from context and what else the writers have said these will have to not take the form of &quot;giant brain&quot; Charms).<br /> 3. Lunars don't tend towards large scale &quot;engineering&quot; projects because their current style (and perhaps this is a bit of a product of a persisting nature) trends them towards being on the run, travelling light and high mobility, &quot;off the grid&quot;.<br /> 4. This said, Lunars don't necessarily make quite as much personal gear for themselves either, because of higher tool independence (just notably more than large scale projects).<br /> 5. They clearly aren't going to outperform Solars at any kind of crafting, even if they wanted to focus the same way, which they wouldn't for reasons. This is not to say that they are bad - they are very good, just that Solars are better at it.<br /> <br /> Hard to argue with any of that. Phrasing Lunar crafting in terms of the restrictions from their present situation and their strengths making certain kinds of gear unnecessary is a lot more useful than saying that it would take away from other splats to have them be good at certain abilities (or Attribute magic doesn't support crafting like it does combat etc.).<br /> <br /> I like the ideas ITT about Lunar crafting power involving personal, authentic, uncontrolled passion and organic qualities (e.g. Gaius's post).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe thing is - the magic of Sol and Luna is drastically different. Anything that needs to be mutable or is made of mutable material falls into the purview of Luna. That Solars could shape the Wyld in 2E was a great mistake in blurring that boundary. Crafting glamour, forging dreams, designing the intelligence behind an A.I - all of these should be areas Lunar excel over all others in. The cut and dry is old and dead 2E stuff. Each field of expertise is more than broad enough for everyone to have a slice of pie - even if that means leaving half the damn thing to Solar's. Sidereals projects would be the best at side-stepping calamity. Dams designed with overflow and such - even if their were a great flood they can duck their fate and survive due to fail safes and preventative measures that far exceed those without eyes on the trials and problems to assail the project in the future (example. Sidereals can simply declare they had some fail safe incorporated when issues arise - retroactively) . Solars are really just about the strongest bridge, the tallest building, the fastest airship - its about excellence and performance and that's all they should be about. This crowding out of themes is a bit ridiculous particularly when the fanon takes over and starts brow beating everyone in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:16:08-08:00","id":11294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=10711#post10711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are &quot;ugly&quot; or &quot;distasteful&quot; going to be descriptive of Lunar magic? I think that sort of organic squick is being concentrated into the Liminal Exalted -- reanimated corpses with Aspects based on substances like blood and soil -- and out of the Lunar Exalted, whose social magic provides &quot;majestic, glorious god-bodies&quot;. Are barbarian beast-gods supposed to be hideous and icky or awe-inspiringly beautiful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how much of Ghost Wolf (from Masters of Jade) would make it across the transition, I'd say there's room for it.<br /> <br /> Still, primal gods can have a tendency to be the least... photogenic in their pantheons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:26:16-08:00","id":11303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=11191#post11191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each field of expertise is more than broad enough for everyone to have a slice of pie - even if that means leaving half the damn thing to Solar's. Sidereals projects would be the best at side-stepping calamity. Dams designed with overflow and such - even if their were a great flood they can duck their fate and survive due to fail safes and preventative measures that far exceed those without eyes on the trials and problems to assail the project in the future (example. Sidereals can simply declare they had some fail safe incorporated when issues arise - retroactively) . Solars are really just about the strongest bridge, the tallest building, the fastest airship - its about excellence and performance and that's all they should be about. This crowding out of themes is a bit ridiculous particularly when the fanon takes over and starts brow beating everyone in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problems with this have been discussed at length, the most straightforward of which is probably &quot;when you portion out things like that, the Solars don't really have anything left&quot;. This is even more of a concern with the introduction of new Exalted.<br /> <br /> Besides, from what I gather, people didn't really take to it too well when Abyssals had &quot;craft really well at ultra-specific things&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to Sidereals, I find the themes behind the Charms they've actually been given to just be more interesting than &quot;craft things that act like they foresee stuff&quot; ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that needs to be mutable or is made of mutable material falls into the purview of Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, but only incidentally, and probably not even that when the system moves away from pools of generic spirit Charms and an idea that part of how you represent powerful gods is by saying &quot;they have their own versions of all of them&quot;.<br /> <br /> The character and panoply of Luna is not one that indicates much of a predilection to such things.<br /> <br /> The Incarnae in general are incidentally related to a bunch of things that it's not really useful to make them the actual gods of, since that cuts away a lot of other gods just by virtue of how big the Incarnae are supposed to be, and likewise it's not really useful to cite those incidentals as ideas for Exalted themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:35:30-08:00","id":11307,"title":"","content":"Solars create permanance, and impose order over Chaos in the same way they impose Holy judgment over Creatures of Darkness. So they surely did need Wyld Shaping Technique.<br /> <br /> Second Edition Lunars, on the other hand, would have been well-served with Charms that imposed Chaos on Creation, and impermanent form on Chaos. Which they may yet get in Third Edition, among their No Moon Shaman Charms. (The power to impose Unholiness on others would also not be remiss.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-15-2013, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:07:27-08:00","id":11326,"title":"","content":"I've generally portrayed Lunar Exalted as being familiar enough with Fair Folk artifice to be able to reverse engineer aspects of it.<br /> For example my version of Ma-Ha-Suchi constructed a Glamour Spell that causes people to exaggerate and embellish his exploits, it served him well as the Wolf with Red Roses and he re-purposed it to protect the Nameless Lair with a terrifying reputation that destroys the morale of enemy armies.<br /> His actual army (in contrast to canon) isn't that big, it's more a devoted group of terrorist skinwalkers (another of his creations) that disrupt supply lines and sow paranoia in the enemy army that the spell then turns up to 11.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:16:08-08:00","id":11708,"title":"","content":"So I don't know if this approach is a valid one, but think about this: From what Holden has posted about Solar Charm philosophy, it seems that he's going with the idea of excellence and perfection in Abilities, but also of Charms that emulate Sol himself. So what if we applied that philosophy to Lunar Charms in that they will be about raw Attributes but will also begin to emulate Luna hirself? In this way, &quot;How would Luna do this?&quot; becomes an important question.<br /> <br /> Given that, I would think that Charm trees might begin to borrow from the various OtherMoons that Luna has devoured/seduced in order to become an actualized being. Now, do we know of a specific OtherMoon that was a craftsman of some sort? I mean did Zatesh craft his scythe? I don't remember all of the proto-Lunas (Lunae?), but perhaps there was one among them that could build things.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? You think that's a useful way to approach this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T18:28:51-08:00","id":11762,"title":"","content":"Hey, it's that one guy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=11708#post11708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that, I would think that Charm trees might begin to borrow from the various OtherMoons that Luna has devoured/seduced in order to become an actualized being.</div> </div> </div> </div>An idea like this came up before, and it led to the statement that the Othermoons are meant to be more about revealing and informing qualities of Luna rather than being alternate power suites that she can assume and/or that Lunars can pursue.<br /> <br /> That Luna was born in such a manner was meant to convey the message of &quot;your patron was the victor in a great game of Battle Royale to decide who gets to be born; you can develop power to be just as canny and enduring and adaptable&quot;. It wasn't &quot;here's a nondescript collection of powers for Luna or her Chosen to have&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe also some themes of &quot;partake of the form and power of what you've defeated&quot; beyond the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean did Zatesh craft his scythe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods don't really craft the iconic elements of their panoplies (excepting maybe those circumstances where it's a god related to crafting, or there's a really big deal in the story behind how they got the item, like a jade whistle made out of your defeated predecessor, or a gift bestowed by an Incarna), they're just kind of intrinsic to their nature, to the point where Black Mirror Shintai automatically equipped you with them.<br /> <br /> The falcastra of Zatesh whose edge pulls the Wyld is just an external embodiment of the power of that god over the Wyld, just as the Godspear of All-Searing Noon or the Blade of Saturn represent qualities and powers of their Incarnae. Luna occasionally wields it because he left a big impact on her personality, but Luna's overall symbolism doesn't really conduct her embodying her powers in a panoply of tools.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T19:51:17-08:00","id":11802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=11762#post11762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, it's that one guy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Heya! I've been absent for awhile, but here I am again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=11762#post11762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea like this came up before, and it led to the statement that the Othermoons are meant to be more about revealing and informing qualities of Luna rather than being alternate power suites that she can assume and/or that Lunars can pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but maybe it's still an idea that Lunar Charms might consist of Attributes + &quot;What Would Luna Do&quot; among other things.<br /> <br /> Hmm .. I'm synergizing with the other thread about Lunars and physicality perhaps going with Luna's propensity for converting raw chaos into fuel for the Daystar could have Lunars being the masters of esoteric raw materials, perhaps by giving ephemeral things (the last breath of the dying, a cat's footsteps, dreams of unborn babies) physical form. I see the eccentric old woman of a No Moon nonchalantly pulling threads of moonlight from the air as if it's just your regular old knitting project.<br /> <br /> Don't mind me, I'm just running my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:40:41-08:00","id":12364,"title":"","content":"Luna and her Exalted Host's relationship with the Wyld is going to depend on what form the Wyld takes in 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> It's no longer a &quot;lava lamp with infinite fairies in it&quot;. I don't know what it's supposed to look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:47:41-08:00","id":12369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=12364#post12364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna and her Exalted Host's relationship with the Wyld is going to depend on what form the Wyld takes in 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> It's no longer a &quot;lava lamp with infinite fairies in it&quot;. I don't know what it's supposed to look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true, so much is changing about Lunar I don't even know what to do while we wait. I doubt core is going to answer too many questions - I really hope the Devs give us a enough lore tidbits (on forums to avoid the decry of word count) that we can at least kit-bash something when 3E drops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T22:31:02-08:00","id":12527,"title":"","content":"Still, what do you think about being able to more easily access/produce esoteric materials as a Lunar crafting specialty? Assuming that esoteric materials even play into the crafting system, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T23:13:16-08:00","id":12547,"title":"","content":"I think it has a lot of merit. For that matter, Claim Territory charms (which I expect to stay personally - tie to Gaia and all) that allow you to manipulate nature so it produces a lot of the raw materials to a more finished and less raw state for you. Trees that grow straight with a preternaturally fine grain, streams pool fine grains of jade dust and other effects as the least gods pay homage.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some form of Bezoar Stone effect that smelts or combines reagents - such could be used for medicine charms as well though. Lotta myths and such about bezoars being cure-alls and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T01:14:35-08:00","id":12577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm synergizing with the other thread about Lunars and physicality perhaps going with Luna's propensity for converting raw chaos into fuel for the Daystar could have Lunars being the masters of esoteric raw materials, perhaps by giving ephemeral things (the last breath of the dying, a cat's footsteps, dreams of unborn babies) physical form. I see the eccentric old woman of a No Moon nonchalantly pulling threads of moonlight from the air as if it's just your regular old knitting project.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure, it seems like it might step on the toes of Raksha... Though now I kinda want an upgrade to Lunar Blade Reconfiguration that lets you pull a temporary moonsilver weapon out of moonlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T06:12:19-08:00","id":12685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=12577#post12577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite sure, it seems like it might step on the toes of Raksha...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except traditionally, Lunars build real artifacts and raksha build glamour artifacts. It doesn't matter if they use the same resources if they produce entirely different goods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T07:13:38-08:00","id":12711,"title":"","content":"There might be occasions where Lunar magic (which might still cover some psychedelic themes) enables a degree of physical interaction with abstractions in a manner that is useful for, among other things, crafting, but it's probably not useful to look on that as a Lunar exclusive, because it's a thing Solars can do as well and there's a lot that's useful for them being able to do so in playing them and composing the setting.<br /> <br /> If Lunars can do it, it's probably helpful to think of the method and possibly the results as something particularly Lunar, in terms of what makes them different over what makes them necessary.<br /> <br /> I think a useful approach to take might not be so much &quot;how does being a Lunar help you be a crafter&quot; so much as &quot;how does being a crafter help you be a Lunar&quot;. Try and think of things Lunars might do and think &quot;how would crafting help with this, and how could it be <u>refined and specified</u> in order to help even more&quot;.<br /> <br /> That idea of Lunars in a good position to improvise and put together stuff quickly and on the move might be a good indication, because it feels inclined to look at crafting fulfilling an aspect of the stated Lunar milieu. It's not about needing a Lunar if you want stuff made that way (although if it serves a particularly Lunar methodology, then it might extend to them having some particular tricks that nobody else have, that can serve them in ways that others couldn't achieve).<br /> <br /> I can kind of imagine a modified backstory for Death at the Root coming from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-17-2013, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T09:55:22-08:00","id":25194,"title":"","content":"I'm a little late to this thread, but what if their crafting has less to do with creating physical tools and weapons, and more to do with crafting mutations and new creatures? Molding the living into something more useful. Crafting gills onto your army, and surprising the enemy by rising out of the river where they least expect you. I'm kind of thinking of a less horrifying Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> They already do it a little bit with their experimental villages and what not, raising beastmen, molding them into a more useful force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1568-dumbo3k","name":"dumbo3k","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T12:22:10-08:00","id":25290,"title":"","content":"I think talking about Lunar craft requires first talkin about Lunar needs.Crafting means tools, and Lunars thanks to their shapeshifting have less needs of manufactured tools such as weapons, armors, vehicles and the like. Likely, their shapeshifting make carrying thinggs around impractical.<br /> Logically, their Craft should be focused on thematically appropriate domains, on tools that will actually be indispensable, or on things that will be easy to carry while shapeshifted or won't need to be carried at all.<br /> I'd see them specializing in building and improving lairs, fortresses, manses, castles and such, as well as creating or transforming other lifeforms to serve or defend them or their interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:21:30-08:00","id":25315,"title":"","content":"They might also prefer &quot;arts&quot; type crafts, such as body-painting, tattooing, piercing... which allows them to kit out their bodies with magical ink in auspicious patterns, Tattoo Artifacts, and Artifact jewelry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T16:51:11-08:00","id":25427,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a charm tree that I thought went along their themes. Least you need your Witch-king charms for your TAW<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/18987-nazgul-charm-tree-taw\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...charm-tree-taw</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T17:37:51-08:00","id":25450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=12711#post12711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because it's a thing Solars can do as well and there's a lot that's useful for them being able to do so in playing them and composing the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe this is going to be accurate anymore, and frankly I support it if it isn't. Solars are changing their themes to emulate more of the UCS's thematic space, that gives them a direct theme that doesn't step on the toes of others. The UCS is one of the least mystical beings, he's a straight up hero, and direct in everything he does. There is no grand intricacy to him, he flat out does things. So it's viable to believe the Solar Exalted are straight up awesome at what they do, but they don't carry the mystical themes with them like manipulating abstractions. Theirs is the charge of flipping the bird on abstractions and imposing order on Chaos. Lunars deal in abstractions and twisting the weapons of enemies upon themselves. They utilize the Wyld rather than breaking it, they take the forms and powers of foes slain,as these are a few of the thematic spaces of Luna. This is what I want from Lunars and Solars, a dichotomy as designed, equal in powers but each in their own ways. Remember Luna is the only god to have looked upon the true face of the UCS and live, emulating his brilliance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:51:23-08:00","id":25497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25450#post25450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are changing their themes to emulate more of the UCS's thematic space</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not changing, John is basing this position on Charms Solars have always had, like Blazing Solar Bolt. Acknowledging and integrating it more readily from the get go just means the already present themes will just have more breadth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">that gives them a direct theme that doesn't step on the toes of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt this is a priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they don't carry the mystical themes with them like manipulating abstractions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean a &quot;manipulation&quot; beyond giving them a form that you can make Artifacts out of?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They utilize the Wyld rather than breaking it....Remember Luna is the only god to have looked upon the true face of the UCS and live, emulating his brilliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:59:44-08:00","id":25500,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25497#post25497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt this is a priority.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It should be, otherwise we get back into the problem that Solars can do everything better than anyone else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25497#post25497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean a &quot;manipulation&quot; beyond giving them a form that you can make Artifacts out of?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, the thematic space of Lunars deals more with manipulating abstractions like objects. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25497#post25497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning a Solar and a Lunar should be equal in power, but in their own directions. Solars of their own brilliance, Lunars in the reflection of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:46:22-08:00","id":25525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25500#post25500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be, otherwise we get back into the problem that Solars can do everything better than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was never a problem. That was always the point.<br /> <br /> Anything a Solar could do, they could do better than anyone else. What's the point of being the Badass Normal of the Exalted, without any gimmicks but Charles Atlas Superpower, if they don't get to embody the narrative of &quot;You Can Beat Anything With Guts and Righteousness&quot;?<br /> <br /> The &quot;only Solars matter&quot; problem was something else entirely; a mistaken philosophy that looked at Solar superiority and deemed everyone else irrelevant. The same philosophy that said mortals didn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:59:09-08:00","id":25534,"title":"","content":"I don't really think each splat should have its own distinctive type of crafting, because it seems unduly confining given the breadth of what craft is, and it exacerbates the focus on miraculous wonder-forging as &quot;real&quot; crafts and implies that your merit as a crafter is a product of the crafting charms you know.<br /> <br /> I think basically everybody should be able to do artifact creation competently, even if Solars remain on a tier by themselves, and if that requires charms, then everybody should have access to those charms. The one really distinctive crafting motif I'd really like to see represented in Lunars is some kind of jury-rigging tricks that allow them to make rickety or short-lived things very quickly out of whatever's on hand, even in cases where the materials available are grossly inappropriate. I wouldn't want that to be the essence of Lunar crafting, but it seems like they're the group best suited to that trick.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;modding&quot; is also a concept space suitable for Lunar Intelligence -- taking an existing creation and tuning it, adding stuff to it, or repurposing it. That seems to broadly conform to Lunar thematics and it's not an ability we've seen before.<br /> <br /> On the whole, though, I think we'll need to wait and see what Lunars are <i>like</i> in 3e. We have a broad sense of their fluff, but even that's a bit vague, and given who's in the current writing team I expect their charms to be much more distinctive than we've seen from them to date, so a lot of the speculation about what Lunars' charmset will look like is kind of moot until we've seen what the corebook has to say about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:01:11-08:00","id":25537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25500#post25500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be, otherwise we get back into the problem that Solars can do everything better than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>More that there's no area in which Solars are weak.<br /> <br /> There's another quality to this, but it's something that probably deserves its own post in its own thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, the thematic space of Lunars deals more with manipulating abstractions like objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that does what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaning a Solar and a Lunar should be equal in power, but in their own directions. Solars of their own brilliance, Lunars in the reflection of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't answer what the relevant distinction between utilizing the Wyld and breaking it is at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:07:54-08:00","id":25542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25525#post25525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was never a problem. That was always the point.<br /> <br /> Anything a Solar could do, they could do better than anyone else. What's the point of being the Badass Normal of the Exalted, without any gimmicks but Charles Atlas Superpower, if they don't get to embody the narrative of &quot;You Can Beat Anything With Guts and Righteousness&quot;?<br /> <br /> The &quot;only Solars matter&quot; problem was something else entirely; a mistaken philosophy that looked at Solar superiority and deemed everyone else irrelevant. The same philosophy that said mortals didn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have no problem if this was the case, but more and more proponents want them to have the fate bending of Sidereals and the shapeshifting of Lunars. Those are the gimmicks of other splats, something a Solar should never be able to do because they don't need to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:13:16-08:00","id":25545,"title":"","content":"I have <i>never</i> seen, or read, anyone I would take seriously ask for those powers. Try again. Less strawman.<br /> <br /> Also, salient point of the game is that, yes, Solars are The Best. It's what they do. There is no one their equal. <i>This is exactly why the Infernal and Abyssal Exalted are so frightening.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:41:05-08:00","id":25555,"title":"","content":"Lunars should have a Stamina charm where they eat the raw materials to an item and poop out the finished work a month later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:41:14-08:00","id":25557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25542#post25542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">more and more proponents want them to have the fate bending of Sidereals and the shapeshifting of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>This tickles me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:35:25-08:00","id":25588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25545#post25545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have <i>never</i> seen, or read, anyone I would take seriously ask for those powers. Try again. Less strawman.<br /> <br /> Also, salient point of the game is that, yes, Solars are The Best. It's what they do. There is no one their equal. <i>This is exactly why the Infernal and Abyssal Exalted are so frightening.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>To expound on this point: the Solar Exalted are terrifying in their own right, something that is obvious from the existence of the legends of the Anathema. <i>Everyone</i> is scared of the Solars coming back, because while they might be here to bring justice and peace and all that good stuff, they might also be here to turn Creation into their sick playground, just like they did towards the waning days of the First Age.<br /> <br /> Now, on top of that, we've got a bunch of Exalted who have all the power of the Solar Exalted and who are apparently loyal to forces that are inimical to Creation itself, and this time around there's no unified front to stop them from wrecking everyone's shit. That the Mask of Winters has already made a beachhead into Creation with Thorns (with a handful of loyal Deathknights spearheading the assault) is simply the first sign of a coming apocalypse, as far as the Powers That Be are concerned. You might understand why some of the folks around Creation might be getting a wee bit antsy, given this situation, don't you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:50:36-08:00","id":25595,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, and I know I've said this before, Lunar craft goes beyond the sharpness of a sword or the balance of an arrow, Lunar crafting is about seeing beyond the purpose of an item to its potential. Lunars are the Wardens at the edge of Creation - a foot in every world and an eye on every horizon. They are about making that sword into something that slices a ghost as well as a man - about an arrow that only feels the heart of its target an ignores all else (wind plows through it without touching it and rain falls around it). Lunar craft is about paintings that crawl into the targets mind and whisper in the back of their brain and about taming the elements beyond the world (Glamor, Vitriol and anything beyond Creation should be their plaything). The sword of the Solar is a *Better* sword, just as the solar is a Better man - the sword of a Lunar is as Other as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:25:37-08:00","id":25623,"title":"","content":"You know what I like about TAW?<br /> <br /> It's right here. It's right there in front of me.<br /> <br /> Lunars 3e will <i>blow</i> TAW out of the water when it comes. But I don't have 3e Lunars, I have <i>speculations</i> of 3e Lunars. I do have TAW though, right in front of me.<br /> <br /> So, I can go look up TAW Crafting charms and I can see exactly what they do, or, if I had the ability, make my own charms within the themes I know about TAW crafting charms, from the charms that I have seen, <i>because they're there.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T12:38:17-08:00","id":25963,"title":"","content":"I considered the idea of the Sacred Hunt being a part of Lunar crafting and my mind instantly went here.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qsFHEK_o9U8\" data-code=\"qsFHEK_o9U8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qsFHEK_o9U8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T15:11:01-08:00","id":26077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25963#post25963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered the idea of the Sacred Hunt being a part of Lunar crafting and my mind instantly went here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less horribly, there's <i>Monster Hunter </i>and the number of improbable weapons and armors that can be made from the mega-fauna of field, mountain, sea and sky.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T03:48:11-08:00","id":26406,"title":"","content":"Silliness aside, I think it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T03:57:04-08:00","id":26409,"title":"","content":"Like this ? Hmmm, I do hate Wood Spider very very much....... &gt;:3<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.minus.com/i4j64yG1Jxa4m.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:34:04-08:00","id":26885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=25588#post25588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To expound on this point: the Solar Exalted are terrifying in their own right, something that is obvious from the existence of the legends of the Anathema. <i>Everyone</i> is scared of the Solars coming back, because while they might be here to bring justice and peace and all that good stuff, they might also be here to turn Creation into their sick playground, just like they did towards the waning days of the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue in the case of what one thinks of when they hear Anathema are Lunars, with Solars being footnotes. Remember the Solars were gone for a very long time, only just re-emerging, and only 150 of them around. Who has been there that whole time, and are 300 strong and can be literally terrifying creatures? Lunars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:53:50-08:00","id":26893,"title":"","content":"You'd be half-right. What the Dragon-Blooded and most of the world think of when they hear Anathema is the Lunar Exalted. What the Sidereal Exalted, especially the elders think of when they hear it is the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> As a Sidereal, or a Terrestrial Exalted, anything that makes Kejak go white with fear, even for a moment, should worry you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:18:52-08:00","id":26915,"title":"","content":"Lunars are indeed the Anathema with which people are most likely to find familiar. They are also the Anathema for which the Wyld Hunt does not typically bring its full might to bear nor always pursue to the death. This is in part because the threat one poses isn't as great (at least not in the same way) and in part because a given Lunar is more likely to be able to finagle her way to a place where the cost and difficulty of pursuit exceed the benefit (what I wouldn't give to find that dev/writer quote &gt;.&gt; ). For the Solar Anathema, that place does not exist: a particularly well-stocked, skilled, armed, and supported Wyld Hunt will move out with all speed and not stop until the Solar is dead.<br /> <br /> No one -- at least no one who's right -- has claimed that Lunars aren't terrifying. They are. They've actually claimed good chunks of Creation among themselves, for crying out loud, and the impression the devs have given is that their brutal, long-term strategy is successfully, gradually grinding the Realm down. But think about what that says about the legends told of the Solar Anathema: as terrifying as Lunars demonstrably are, Solars are <i>still</i> prioritized above them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:22:54-08:00","id":27751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=26915#post26915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are indeed the Anathema with which people are most likely to find familiar. They are also the Anathema for which the Wyld Hunt does not typically bring its full might to bear nor always pursue to the death. This is in part because the threat one poses isn't as great (at least not in the same way) and in part because a given Lunar is more likely to be able to finagle her way to a place where the cost and difficulty of pursuit exceed the benefit (what I wouldn't give to find that dev/writer quote &gt;.&gt; ). For the Solar Anathema, that place does not exist: a particularly well-stocked, skilled, armed, and supported Wyld Hunt will move out with all speed and not stop until the Solar is dead.<br /> <br /> No one -- at least no one who's right -- has claimed that Lunars aren't terrifying. They are. They've actually claimed good chunks of Creation among themselves, for crying out loud, and the impression the devs have given is that their brutal, long-term strategy is successfully, gradually grinding the Realm down. But think about what that says about the legends told of the Solar Anathema: as terrifying as Lunars demonstrably are, Solars are <i>still</i> prioritized above them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would think an enemy that can literally be anyone, and come out of nowhere, whose known for killing and taking the forms of others is a higher priority than the legend of terrible god-kings and their supposed return. I'm not saying Solars are seen as less of a threat, but that their threat is in their legend, the tales told about them. the Lunar threat was less a legend and more the local news, it was a real thing for a very long time whereas the Solars were gone from the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:02:14-08:00","id":27949,"title":"","content":"Except Kejop Chejak is calling the shots, and he very well remembers that the Solars are the bigger threat. A Lunar Exalt <i>can</i> be a greater immediate threat than a Solar Exalt. But any Solar Exalt can and usually <i>will</i> be a greater <i>long-term</i> threat than any Lunar. Chejop does not dare ever allow a Solar to survive long enough to become a long-term threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:05:59-08:00","id":27981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=27751#post27751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying Solars are seen as less of a threat, but that their threat is in their legend, the tales told about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And occasionally the Solar warlord who slips the net of the Wyld Hunt and the Realm has to make war against him for ten years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:30:08-08:00","id":27995,"title":"","content":"And not just a skirmish. The last time before the Bull of the North clusterfuck, it was the entire armies of the Realm vs ONE Dawn Caste and the armies he managed to raise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:05:23-08:00","id":28067,"title":"","content":"Yeah, prior canon and dev remarks for EX3 paint a pretty clear picture of the priorities involved, re: preventing large-scale threats. At the same time, as I said, it's not to say Lunars aren't threatening. Nobody is claiming that when the Wyld Hunt corners an Anathema and they see the silver anima banner, they all heave a collective sigh of relief and the Dragonblooded start packing up their things; maybe let the mortal stableboys take care of it so they can break a sweat. Lunars are still something they take very seriously. And the terror most of Creation has of them <i>may </i>be more widespread if that was your meaning. Even for someone who knows the full extent of the Solar threat, the odds that someone's life and livelihood may be wrecked by a Solar have historically been much lower than the odds for a Lunar. That definitely means a more <i>personal</i> terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:19:08-08:00","id":29744,"title":"","content":"Enough Solars, this is a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> One approach is to pull on the Lunars' themes of personal closeness and empathy. A Solar can make a generic Ultimate Sword. A Sidereal can use their fatecrafting to make a sword that's perfectly suited for one particular task, like slaying a tyrant. But a Lunar makes a sword that's perfectly suited for some<i>one</i>. No conditions, no demands attached to it, just a weapon that perfectly suits their fighting style. They can use it however they'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:47:23-08:00","id":29757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SurlySeraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=29744#post29744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enough Solars, this is a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> One approach is to pull on the Lunars' themes of personal closeness and empathy. A Solar can make a generic Ultimate Sword. A Sidereal can use their fatecrafting to make a sword that's perfectly suited for one particular task, like slaying a tyrant. But a Lunar makes a sword that's perfectly suited for some<i>one</i>. No conditions, no demands attached to it, just a weapon that perfectly suits their fighting style. They can use it however they'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that too. Lunars are all about the physical and stuff - adapting and their own body. We have charms that grow shields and engulf weapons with your own flesh to prevent being disarmed - it make sense to make a weapon not as a weapon but as a part of the bearers body. Making charms that mind screwy...I'll leave to someone else *for now*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T23:22:18-08:00","id":29769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=29757#post29757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that too. Lunars are all about the physical and stuff - adapting and their own body. We have charms that grow shields and engulf weapons with your own flesh to prevent being disarmed - it make sense to make a weapon not as a weapon but as a part of the bearers body. Making charms that mind screwy...I'll leave to someone else *for now*.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gr66YIoR5Os\" target=\"_blank\">Last Warrior's Unity?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T04:16:13-08:00","id":29829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SurlySeraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=29744#post29744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One approach is to pull on the Lunars' themes of personal closeness and empathy. A Solar can make a generic Ultimate Sword. A Sidereal can use their fatecrafting to make a sword that's perfectly suited for one particular task, like slaying a tyrant. But a Lunar makes a sword that's perfectly suited for some<i>one</i>. No conditions, no demands attached to it, just a weapon that perfectly suits their fighting style. They can use it however they'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference?<br /> <br /> More importantly, how and why do Solars have some kind of mental block against making more than one kind of sword, or specifying a sword to a particular person?<br /> <br /> And what does the &quot;perfectly suited to slaying tyrant&quot; sword do? More importantly, what does it do when faced by not-a-tyrant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-14-2013, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T20:28:51-08:00","id":30721,"title":"","content":"It's not that they can't do what the others can, it's that each splat has a particular style which they lend themselves to. Solars are good at power and perfection, so their magical weapons tend to be very powerful and a perfect example of its kind. Sidereals do the fate-thing; their most powerful works of artifice are created when they imbue it with a Destiny - a magical sword can still be powerful against other foes, but against that one foe it was destined to fell, it can equal or even outmatch the greatest of Solar blades. And Lunars, instead, tie their weapons to people, like how they are bound, how their patron is bound; depending on the Lunar and the weapon, a sword might be perfect for an Exaltation - frequently, the Lunar's mate - or it might be tied to the soul of the person the Lunar cares about. To others, it is still a powerful artefact, but when wielded by the one it was made for, it is greater still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:33:21-08:00","id":35657,"title":"","content":"One idea I had for Lunars is a cross between MacGyver and the &quot;make stuff up from Wyld&quot; of the Fair Folk: the Lunars can make short term items out of anything. An axe made of silk that cuts as well as steel, a flute of grass, a shield of air.... things that are not craftable for even a Solar without serious sorcery backing them up or a Fair Folk drawing on its impossible power are at the tip of the fingers for a Lunar. Just as their shape can be matched for the occasion, so can they shape and mold their environment for their benefit, <i>literally</i>. At higher levels I can see cloaks of shadow and fortresses of fur and wood and bone... as long as it's something of an elemental material, something from Gaia and Creation, it can be shaped for a purpose. Maybe play it up as Luna's mercurial teaching meeting Gaia's stalwart substance or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:58:52-08:00","id":35709,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I'm starting to get annoyed with folks saying &quot;X Splat should have MacGyver powers!&quot; It's been said of nearly every splat, yet even <i>what &quot;MacGyver&quot; means</i> seems to vary with each poster.<br /> <br /> You want to whip together a useful tool in no time out of stuff you've got sitting around? That's a goddamned stunt; using chocolate to neutralize acid shouldn't require you be a Lunar with Duck Tape Atemi.<br /> <br /> Also, Terrestrials and Fair Folk are currently the kings of MacGyver-ing; a Terrestrial can use his hands as tools and kick together an item out of its component pieces, where a Fair Folk can Wyld stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:30:23-08:00","id":35810,"title":"","content":"The themes of Lunar Crafting?<br /> <br /> Sucking, mostly. <br /> <br /> I'm only half-kidding there. Basically, there is basically no way you could make Lunars actually be able to craft in any sense that is meaningful to an actual campaign (no, &quot;they're not useless at crafting, they can craft as well as a mortal if they take the years to do it&quot; is not an argument that passes muster when compared to the realities of gameplay) without people complaining that it's just ripping off solars (to wit, this thread). In addition, the backstory mostly requires Lunars to <i>not </i>be good at crafting things in order to make sense. And everything I've heard from the devs about the tone of new Lunars seems more concerned with tearing down than building up, theme wise, so that's another thematic impediment. <br /> <br /> All in all, I'm mostly expecting that the game's response if you want to play a Lunar artisan is still going to be &quot;go play a Solar, silly&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:42:28-08:00","id":35816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=35709#post35709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I'm starting to get annoyed with folks saying &quot;X Splat should have MacGyver powers!&quot; It's been said of nearly every splat, yet even <i>what &quot;MacGyver&quot; means</i> seems to vary with each poster.<br /> <br /> You want to whip together a useful tool in no time out of stuff you've got sitting around? That's a goddamned stunt; using chocolate to neutralize acid shouldn't require you be a Lunar with Duck Tape Atemi.<br /> <br /> Also, Terrestrials and Fair Folk are currently the kings of MacGyver-ing; a Terrestrial can use his hands as tools and kick together an item out of its component pieces, where a Fair Folk can Wyld stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument is perhaps less &quot;they should have MacGyvering&quot; and more &quot;nobody else should focus on immediate result with their Charms like Lunars do.&quot; Lunars really ought to have a Charm suite that allows them to ignore non-magical material requirements, tool requirements, typical crafting time, and so forth so they can literally produce things from thin air.<br /> <br /> Basically, they should be able to ignore the normal tedium of crafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:46:53-08:00","id":35820,"title":"","content":".... Why?<br /> <br /> /10char","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:41:48-08:00","id":35856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, there is basically no way you could make Lunars actually be able to craft in any sense that is meaningful to an actual campaign (no, &quot;they're not useless at crafting, they can craft as well as a mortal if they take the years to do it&quot; is not an argument that passes muster when compared to the realities of gameplay)</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you talking exclusively about Artifacts? I've said elsewhere about how I think a decent chunk of what's useful in Crafts amounts to every improvised, non-offensive use of Bending in Avatar. On that note, the immense strength of a Lunar is probably helpful in digging gigantic ditches to redirect lava. That doesn't mean that Lunars should have &quot;dig gigantic ditches with their bare hands&quot; Charms, but it contributes to the image of what a Lunar using Crafts would look like. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, the backstory mostly requires Lunars to not be good at crafting things in order to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not on the scale of the First Age, maybe, but if they crafted whatever's running the destiny of the Caul... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly expecting that the game's response if you want to play a Lunar artisan is still going to be &quot;go play a Solar, silly&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> What do you imagine would be entailed in playing a Lunar artisan that would make such a response apparent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T03:54:30-08:00","id":36289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=35856#post35856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are you talking exclusively about Artifacts? I've said elsewhere about how I think a decent chunk of what's useful in Crafts amounts to every improvised, non-offensive use of Bending in Avatar. On that note, the immense strength of a Lunar is probably helpful in digging gigantic ditches to redirect lava. That doesn't mean that Lunars should have &quot;dig gigantic ditches with their bare hands&quot; Charms, but it contributes to the image of what a Lunar using Crafts would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I on the other hand would disagree a fair bit. It would never occur to me to require a craft roll out of someone to dig a ditch. I mean, it's just shoveling. A big Lunar has a much bigger shovel, but building ditches is a thing that I would allow any character to do if I was GMing. It's not a thing that helps define a character as someone who <i>makes </i>things, which is generally what I think of when thinking of &quot;an artisan&quot;. Craft characters make things, one way or another. It can be perishable, spur of the moment stuff, or it can be lasting things, but there has to be a thing, and a thing that is<i> left better </i>for the character having worked on it. <br /> <br /> And I figure most of the build things out of elements available thing is probably still going to be the DB Craft shchtick (is that spelled right?). I mean, I wouldn't be opposed to such things, I just don't really imagine they're going to be taken away from DBs to build up Lunars. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=35856#post35856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not on the scale of the First Age, maybe, but if they crafted whatever's running the destiny of the Caul...</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fully expecting the Caul to be a labor of many, many years and much blood and sweat. I even acknowledge anything else probably would not even be <i>appropriate</i>. The Caul is a very important thing and a bastion against the largest forces arrayed against the Lunars, it <i>can't</i> have been easy nor be eternal. And that's good! But it says nothing about a Lunar's ability to actually be playable as someone who makes things in an actual on-a-table campaign. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=35856#post35856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you imagine would be entailed in playing a Lunar artisan that would make such a response apparent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, if there is no real support for a Lunar making things beyond the same basic ability everyone gets. If a big part of your character concept is &quot;artisan&quot; you kind of want to be <i>especially </i>good at making stuff, by definition, in the same way that if a big part of your character concept is &quot;combatant&quot; you probably won't be satisfied with maxing the Melee or Martial Arts Ability, you'll probably want some extra tricks to make you <i>especially </i>good at it. And from what I've read from the devs, I generally don't expect that Lunar mojo is going to head in a direction that helps with Craft, in general. I'll be happy if I'm wrong, but for now, that's my speculation, as baseless as every other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T04:51:46-08:00","id":36300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/9451-lunar-craft-themes?p=36289#post36289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I on the other hand would disagree a fair bit. It would never occur to me to require a craft roll out of someone to dig a ditch. I mean, it's just shoveling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really; not if it's a ditch constructed towards the purpose that ditches are actually intended for.<br /> <br /> Like, in this instance, it's not only a furrow in the earth, it also has to be shaped specifically enough to redirect a lava flow and making sure that the walls don't cave into the opened space.<br /> <br /> It might not look so sophisticated to the layman, but a pyramid is just bricks stacked on top of one another to a layman as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T01:58:16-08:00","id":36827,"title":"","content":"My favorite Lunar craft charm from previous editions allowed them to restructure materials simply by passing their hands over it, making any substance like soft clay in thier hands. That always seemed to be the essence of lunar crafting to me. Where a solar can make the absolutely most amazing wonders when they amass enough infrastructure and support (and whatever else is deemed necessary), a Lunar can take nearly any item at hand and adapt it to be just what he/she needs for the situation.<br /> <br /> SO a solar can craft several weapons of unparallelled power to be ready for any battle that may arise. A lunar, on the other hand, only brings a walking stick to any fight... and has a damn fine daiklaive, bow, shield, axe or what have you from that one item alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1027-deamion","name":"Deamion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1027_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}